1
00:00:02,214 --> 00:00:07,330
The Life Of Muhammadﷺ, The Madinan Period, Volume 2

2
00:00:07,827 --> 00:00:09,831
By Imam Anwar Al_Awlaki,

3
00:00:10,804 --> 00:00:13,397
اَعُوْذُ بِاللهِ مِنَّ الشِّيْطَانِ الرَّجِيْمِ ۝بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمَانِ الرَّحِيْمَ۝

4
00:00:14,054 --> 00:00:19,962
اَلْحَمْدُ لله ، وَالصَّلَاةُ وَالسَّلَامُ عَلى سَيِّدِنَا محمد وَعَلَى اَلِهِ وَصَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ تَسْلِيْمًا كَثِيْرا

5
00:00:20,990 --> 00:00:27,135
Tayyib(طيب), we will begin In Sha Allah Ta'ala(إِنْ شَاءالله تعالى) with some events from the sixth year of Hijrah(هجرة),

6
00:00:27,568 --> 00:00:31,778
before we move on to the story of Ibn-Al-Aqwa(اِبْنِ الْاَكْوَع).

7
00:00:32,249 --> 00:00:34,323
This event is mentioned in Sahih Al-Bukhari(صحيح ألبخاري)

8
00:00:35,096 --> 00:00:40,840
some men from the tribe of Uqul(عُقُل), and in one narration Urayna(عُرَيْنَةْ),

9
00:00:41,598 --> 00:00:44,923
these narrations are in Bukhari(بخاريْ) and Muslim(مسلم) and some other books of Hadith(حديث)

10
00:00:45,237 --> 00:00:48,452
also mentioned in the books of Seerah(سيرة) by Ibn Is'haaq(إبن إسحاق) and Al-Waqadie(ألواقعدي).

11
00:00:49,113 --> 00:00:51,358
Anyway so the narration is authentic.

12
00:00:51,957 --> 00:00:54,829
These are men, some narrations say that, they're eight of them.

13
00:00:55,320 --> 00:00:58,847
They were extremely poor suffering from malnutrition.

14
00:00:59,525 --> 00:01:02,274
So, they came to Rasool Allah ﷺ and they came to Madina

15
00:01:02,298 --> 00:01:04,654
they were from outside Madina, they were Bedouins.

16
00:01:05,414 --> 00:01:09,258
They came to Madina and they accepted Islam and they were asking for Sadaqah(صدقه).

17
00:01:10,114 --> 00:01:13,189
They became Muslim in Madina and they stayed with Ahlus-Suffah(إهل الصفه).

18
00:01:13,349 --> 00:01:18,194
Ahlus-Suffah(إهل الصفه), I think we talked about them before in the initial stage of Madina.

19
00:01:18,571 --> 00:01:24,073
Towards the back of Al-Masjid-Al-Nabawi(ألمسجد النبوي) there was a place that was shaded from the sun.

20
00:01:24,282 --> 00:01:31,137
In which the homeless or poor of the Sahabah(صحابه) from the Muhajireen(مهاجرين), who have nowhere to stay.

21
00:01:31,423 --> 00:01:37,676
They would stay in that place and the Ansaar(انصار) would bring food to them, or would invite them.

22
00:01:38,182 --> 00:01:41,414
So, you would have one Ansaari(أنصاري) take one of them with him

23
00:01:41,439 --> 00:01:42,592
some of them would take two,

24
00:01:42,837 --> 00:01:45,124
then you have people like Saad Bin Ubadah(سعدبن عبادة) they would take 10,

25
00:01:45,613 --> 00:01:51,237
they would take 10 men from Ahlus-Suffah(إهل الصفه) and would invite them.

26
00:01:51,887 --> 00:01:55,815
Anyway so these eight men they became Muslim and they stayed with Ahlus-Suffah(إهل الصفه).

27
00:01:56,319 --> 00:01:57,909
فَاسْتَوْخَمُوا الْمَدِيْنَهْ

28
00:01:57,934 --> 00:02:00,500
They were feeling unhealthy

29
00:02:01,150 --> 00:02:08,578
and this is something well known about Madina at that time, the climate of Madina was unhealthy.

30
00:02:09,097 --> 00:02:11,993
In one narration, Ayesha رضي الله عنها said;

31
00:02:12,033 --> 00:02:18,170
When they first made Hijrah(هجرة) to Madina that they suffered bouts of fever

32
00:02:18,690 --> 00:02:24,474
and she said, that this area called Bat'haan(بطحان), it was full of stagnant water.

33
00:02:24,906 --> 00:02:30,805
So, Allah-Ho-Alam(الله اعلم) is this a Malaria related fever or is it Typhoid, what exactly is it?

34
00:02:30,829 --> 00:02:34,312
Is it a bacterial infections, viral infections? Allah-Ho-Alam(الله اعلم)

35
00:02:34,604 --> 00:02:36,799
but diseases were endemic to Madina.

36
00:02:37,303 --> 00:02:41,478
And these eight men, who came to Madina,

37
00:02:41,689 --> 00:02:47,312
by the way, we also talked about for example some lines of poetry from Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) and Bilal(بلال)

38
00:02:47,677 --> 00:02:54,359
when they came to Madina, they all became extremely ill with a very strong fevers.

39
00:02:54,655 --> 00:02:57,714
Well, anyway these eight men who came into Madina,

40
00:02:58,218 --> 00:03:03,314
they didn't like the climate, it wasn't befitting of their constitution,

41
00:03:03,354 --> 00:03:07,699
 so they asked Rasool Allah ﷺ and then said that,

42
00:03:07,731 --> 00:03:09,552
اِنَّا اُنَاس الزَرْعَ

43
00:03:10,133 --> 00:03:12,868
وَلَمْ نَكُنْ اَهل الْرِيْفْ وَاستوْخَمْنَا الْمَدِيْنَةْ

44
00:03:13,135 --> 00:03:15,865
They said: We are people, who are shepherds

45
00:03:16,658 --> 00:03:22,151
and we are not people, urban people, Ahl Ar-Reif(أهل ألريف), or people who are settled

46
00:03:22,784 --> 00:03:25,532
and Madina is unhealthy for us.

47
00:03:26,261 --> 00:03:27,731
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ told them;

48
00:03:27,771 --> 00:03:34,747
Well then I will give you permission to go out with my shepherd outside of Madina

49
00:03:35,468 --> 00:03:44,882
and I order you to drink, from the milk and urine, of the camels of Sadaqah(صدقه).

50
00:03:45,424 --> 00:03:50,749
So they went out and they started drinking from the milk of the camels

51
00:03:50,789 --> 00:03:55,751
and the urine of these camels until they became healthy.

52
00:03:56,219 --> 00:03:57,945
And it says, in one narration;

53
00:03:58,183 --> 00:03:59,688
فَعَدَتَ اِلَيْهِمْ اَلْوَنُهُمْ

54
00:03:59,713 --> 00:04:02,587
So, their natural color came back to them.

55
00:04:03,453 --> 00:04:07,738
Because this is might be one indication that they were suffering from jaundice

56
00:04:07,763 --> 00:04:11,784
or some liver disease which caused their colors to change, Allah-Ho-Alam(الله اعلم).

57
00:04:12,296 --> 00:04:18,215
And now, after drinking the milk and urine of these camels, they became healthy again.

58
00:04:19,100 --> 00:04:25,143
Well after becoming healthy, they were ungrateful, what they did is

59
00:04:25,168 --> 00:04:32,456
They killed the shepherd of Rasool Allah ﷺ and they stole the camels

60
00:04:33,186 --> 00:04:39,158
and they became Murtadd(مرتد), they have given up Islam and they fled.

61
00:04:39,981 --> 00:04:44,667
This was in return to the generosity of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

62
00:04:45,128 --> 00:04:46,840
The news reached to Rasool Allah ﷺ.

63
00:04:46,879 --> 00:04:49,864
فَاَرْسَلَ فِي طَّلَبِهِمْ فَلَمْ تَرتفعِ الشَّمْسْ حَتَّى اَتَى بِهِمْ

64
00:04:50,477 --> 00:04:52,137
The news reach to Rasool Allah ﷺ

65
00:04:52,177 --> 00:04:56,533
and by the time the sun was rising, they were already brought back.

66
00:04:56,766 --> 00:05:00,033
And it says that Rasool Allah ﷺ made a Dua(دُعَا) against them.

67
00:05:00,263 --> 00:05:05,546
اَللَّهُمَّ عَمِّ عَلَيْهِمْ الطَّرِيْقْ وَجَعَلْهَا عَلَيْهِمْ اَضِّيق مِنْ مِّسْكِ جَمَلْ

68
00:05:05,949 --> 00:05:11,784
Rasool Allah ﷺ made a Dua(دُعَا) against them, to blind them, and to make their paths narrow.

69
00:05:12,273 --> 00:05:14,649
So, they became lost and they were brought back

70
00:05:14,689 --> 00:05:19,685
and in one narration from Seerah(سيرة) it says, that when the news reach to Rasool Allah ﷺ

71
00:05:19,916 --> 00:05:23,586
He was sitting with 20 young men from Al-Ansaar(ألأنصار)

72
00:05:23,756 --> 00:05:29,033
and these are the ones, whom Rasool Allah ﷺ dispatched, to bring back these robbers.

73
00:05:29,707 --> 00:05:32,551
What did Rasool Allah ﷺ do? How did he treat them?

74
00:05:32,887 --> 00:05:35,323
It says in this narration, by Bukhari(بخاريْ),

75
00:05:35,718 --> 00:05:40,670
فَاَمَرَبِمَسَامِيْرَ، وَاُحْمِيَّتْ فَكَوَاهُمْ بِهَا

76
00:05:41,135 --> 00:05:47,825
He ordered that, their eyes be branded by hot iron nails,

77
00:05:48,267 --> 00:05:50,883
وَقَطَّعَ اَيْدِيَهُمْ وَاَرْجُلَهُمْ

78
00:05:51,286 --> 00:05:56,709
And he severed their arms, and their legs,

79
00:05:56,877 --> 00:06:01,221
وَاَلْقَاهُمْ فِيْ الّحَرَّةِ يَسْتَسْقُوْنَ فلَا يُسْقَوْنْ

80
00:06:01,476 --> 00:06:03,187
And he left them in a Al-Harr'ra(ألحره),

81
00:06:03,402 --> 00:06:11,454
Al-Harr'ra(ألحره) is an area next to my Madina volcanic, tracks, covered with black volcanic rocks.

82
00:06:11,868 --> 00:06:15,115
This is Al-Harr'ra(ألحره) it's right next to Madina,

83
00:06:15,305 --> 00:06:19,075
they were left there and they would ask for water to drink

84
00:06:19,099 --> 00:06:21,313
and they would not be provided with it.

85
00:06:21,732 --> 00:06:23,912
حَتَّى مَاتُوا وَلَمْ يَحْسِمهُمْ

86
00:06:24,084 --> 00:06:25,340
Until they died,

87
00:06:25,602 --> 00:06:26,563
وَلَمْ يَحْسِمَهُمْ,

88
00:06:26,603 --> 00:06:29,966
 Al-Hasm(اَلْحسم) when, the limb is severed

89
00:06:30,466 --> 00:06:35,135
they would use boiling oil to stop the flow of blood to stop the bleeding.

90
00:06:35,565 --> 00:06:40,558
In their case, this was not done to them, so they bled till death.

91
00:06:41,398 --> 00:06:43,060
Three points to make on this Hadith(حديث).

92
00:06:43,528 --> 00:06:48,315
Number one, using urine, is urine Najs(نجس) or Tahir(طاهر)?

93
00:06:48,851 --> 00:06:52,444
So what's the Fiqh(فقه) of it, without going into much detail

94
00:06:52,924 --> 00:06:55,334
one could refer to the books of Fiqh(فقه) for this.

95
00:06:55,963 --> 00:06:58,431
Some scholars based on this Hadith(حديث),

96
00:06:59,047 --> 00:07:04,920
they Hukm(حكم) that the urine and dung of edible animals is Tahir(طاهر)

97
00:07:05,724 --> 00:07:08,242
and these are Malik(مالك) and Ahmad(أحمد).

98
00:07:08,319 --> 00:07:10,713
Imam Ahmad(اِمَامْ اَحْمَدْ) and Imam Malik(اِمِام مَالِك), this is their opinion.

99
00:07:11,443 --> 00:07:14,933
While the rest of the Ulema(علماء) see that it is Najs(نجس).

100
00:07:15,758 --> 00:07:20,598
Number two, using urine, as a cure as a medicine.

101
00:07:21,133 --> 00:07:24,141
This has been a controversial issue,

102
00:07:24,212 --> 00:07:32,743
and the non believers have used this, as a gate in which they would attack Hadith(حديث) through.

103
00:07:33,200 --> 00:07:38,699
And also the ones who reject Hadith(حديث) and try to discredit Bukhari(بخاريْ) and Muslim(مسلم).

104
00:07:39,086 --> 00:07:46,595
They also use this Hadith(حديث) as, an attacking point against the Hadith(حديث) of Rasool Allah ﷺ

105
00:07:46,734 --> 00:07:52,747
and the disbelievers made the big deal about this issue of using urine as a medicine.

106
00:07:53,046 --> 00:07:57,428
Now, I don't want to go into a lot of details regarding this point.

107
00:07:57,458 --> 00:08:04,099
But just briefly because it's outside the context of Seerah(سيرة) just briefly, I would like to say that

108
00:08:04,618 --> 00:08:09,772
urine has been used as medicine in many cultures around the world.

109
00:08:10,261 --> 00:08:16,927
And even in modern medicine, it is used as an ingredient in some drugs

110
00:08:17,299 --> 00:08:20,566
for example, there's a drug called Premarin

111
00:08:21,031 --> 00:08:28,200
and this is the commercial name for a compound drug consisting primarily of conjugated estrogens.

112
00:08:28,356 --> 00:08:32,156
I mean, this quote I'm reading it from Wikipedia,

113
00:08:32,754 --> 00:08:39,239
isolated from mares urine, it is manufactured by YES pharmaceuticals

114
00:08:39,610 --> 00:08:42,638
and has been marketed since 1942.

115
00:08:43,033 --> 00:08:45,975
So, from 1942 until now, until today

116
00:08:46,268 --> 00:08:49,642
this drug is widely prescribed, and it's still used.

117
00:08:49,682 --> 00:08:56,902
And it says, Premarin has been one of the most widely used drugs in the United States.

118
00:08:57,078 --> 00:09:03,609
So, if there are medicational benefits in a particular ingredient in urine

119
00:09:03,787 --> 00:09:08,442
then modern medicine does not see any problem in using it

120
00:09:08,845 --> 00:09:15,647
but because it is mentioned in Bukhari(بخاريْ) and Muslim(مسلم) and attributed to Muhammadﷺ it's a big deal.

121
00:09:16,156 --> 00:09:20,530
Without testing the validity of the prescription,

122
00:09:20,994 --> 00:09:24,805
without looking into whether it is beneficial or not

123
00:09:25,106 --> 00:09:28,911
they are attacking with preconceived notions.

124
00:09:29,269 --> 00:09:32,823
Now, as a Muslim we should believe in it

125
00:09:32,848 --> 00:09:36,052
as long as the Sanad(سند) of it is authentic and that's the case.

126
00:09:36,550 --> 00:09:41,629
I mean we don't have to test it pharmaceutically and to prove the benefit of it

127
00:09:41,653 --> 00:09:46,704
as long as Rasool Allah ﷺ said so... We believe it, that's the position of the Muslims.

128
00:09:47,216 --> 00:09:53,250
But what the non Muslims, they should have put this to trial and experimented with it

129
00:09:53,645 --> 00:09:56,733
before attacking the Muslims for it.

130
00:09:56,939 --> 00:10:00,089
And there are some research papers that were done

131
00:10:00,334 --> 00:10:06,013
on the anti viral qualities of camel urine

132
00:10:06,361 --> 00:10:10,769
and the fact that it might have on the liver

133
00:10:11,062 --> 00:10:16,072
and one can refer back to these research papers for more details.

134
00:10:16,420 --> 00:10:22,029
The thing is that, it says in the Hadith(حديث), that they were cured from the disease that they had.

135
00:10:22,833 --> 00:10:27,099
And one can use the different narrations, I mean, someone with medical background

136
00:10:27,505 --> 00:10:34,795
can use the different narrations to try to find, leads to what particular disease these people sufferred from.

137
00:10:35,062 --> 00:10:37,795
I recall that in one narration, I think it's in Muslim(مسلم)

138
00:10:38,064 --> 00:10:41,084
it says that they suffered from a digestive disease.

139
00:10:41,412 --> 00:10:44,834
But in another one, it says that their colors changed.

140
00:10:44,874 --> 00:10:50,331
So, it could be jaundice something or it could be hepatitis or some problem with the liver.

141
00:10:50,687 --> 00:10:56,230
Anyway, one can compile all of the different narrations and try to find out what the disease is

142
00:10:56,385 --> 00:11:02,801
and then make an experiment on the different ingredients of camel urine,

143
00:11:02,841 --> 00:11:09,071
to see how, it healed them from that particular disease that, they suffered from.

144
00:11:10,059 --> 00:11:16,946
The third point is the extreme punishment that these men were subjected to.

145
00:11:17,434 --> 00:11:18,959
Brothers and Sisters,

146
00:11:19,221 --> 00:11:23,752
we never find in the Seerah(سيرة) of Rasool Allah ﷺ before this event, or after this event

147
00:11:24,019 --> 00:11:28,220
any punishment similar to the punishment that these men were subjected to.

148
00:11:28,529 --> 00:11:29,701
So, the question is why?

149
00:11:30,064 --> 00:11:36,214
why was this particularly severe punishment prescribed by Rasool Allah ﷺ.?

150
00:11:36,239 --> 00:11:41,919
And also, this is a point that, the disbelievers use against Muhammadﷺ

151
00:11:42,413 --> 00:11:47,637
to try to prove, so called violence that is in the Sunnah(سنة) in Islam.

152
00:11:48,235 --> 00:11:53,524
Well as I mentioned, we never find anything similar to it, before or after.

153
00:11:53,966 --> 00:11:58,000
This is the only time, in which we find such a severe punishment occurring

154
00:11:58,316 --> 00:12:02,379
Abu Qalabah(أبوقلابة) one of the narrators of the Hadith(حديث), which is Al-Bukhari(ألبخاري)

155
00:12:02,925 --> 00:12:05,780
he said, after mentioning the Hadith(حديث), he said;

156
00:12:06,014 --> 00:12:12,285
فَهولآءِ قَتَلُوا وَسَرَقُوْا وَكَفَرُوْا بَعْدَ اِيْمَانِهِمْ وَحَارَبُوا الله وَرَسُوْلَه

157
00:12:12,878 --> 00:12:21,419
He says; These men, they murdered and they stole, and they disbelieved, after believing

158
00:12:21,791 --> 00:12:25,217
and they fought against Allah and His Messenger.

159
00:12:25,495 --> 00:12:30,574
So, all of these crimes, combined, justified that punishment,

160
00:12:31,234 --> 00:12:36,205
because all of these are severe crimes, murder, and then you have stealing

161
00:12:36,442 --> 00:12:39,381
and then you have Riddah(ردة) and then we have Hirabah(حرابة)

162
00:12:39,721 --> 00:12:43,912
which is armed robbery, and this carries a very severe punishment

163
00:12:43,937 --> 00:12:50,093
which is mentioned, in Qur'an that one arm should be cut off and one foot should be cut off.

164
00:12:50,926 --> 00:12:52,638
And in Hadith(حديث), Al-Muslim(اَلْمُسلم)

165
00:12:53,032 --> 00:12:56,484
he says that, the reason why their eyes were branded,

166
00:12:56,524 --> 00:13:01,204
is because they branded the eyes of the shepherd of Rasool Allah ﷺ, Yasa'ar(يَسار).

167
00:13:01,692 --> 00:13:06,236
So, in Muslim(مسلم) it says that, the reason why their eyes were branded is

168
00:13:06,276 --> 00:13:09,188
 because they branded the eyes of the shepherd.

169
00:13:09,481 --> 00:13:15,330
So, they were treated Bil-Misl(بالمثل), they were treated equally, Qisaas(قصاص), retribution.

170
00:13:15,471 --> 00:13:18,205
Also Ibn Hajar(إبن حجر) comments that some of the Ulema(علماء),

171
00:13:18,229 --> 00:13:23,947
some of the Ulema(علماء) see that this Hukum(حكم), this punishment is abrogated, Mansookh(منسوخ).

172
00:13:24,232 --> 00:13:25,576
Qatadah(قتادة) says;

173
00:13:25,601 --> 00:13:32,440
بَلَغَنَا اَنَّ رَسُوْل الله صلى الله عليه وسلم كَانَ اِذَ خَطَبَ بَعْدَ ذَالِكْ اَمَرَ بِصَدَقَة وَنَهَى عنِ الْمُثْلَهْ

174
00:13:32,559 --> 00:13:36,556
Qatadah(قتادة) used to say we were told that Rasool Allah ﷺ after that

175
00:13:37,053 --> 00:13:40,563
if he gives a Khut'ba(خطبة), he would encourage people to give Sadaqah(صدقه)

176
00:13:40,763 --> 00:13:44,856
and he would prohibit them, from mutilation, from maiming

177
00:13:45,422 --> 00:13:49,677
but this is not an agreed upon opinion, it's one opinion that this has been abrogated

178
00:13:49,702 --> 00:13:52,447
some of the Ulema(علماء) say that it's not abrogated

179
00:13:52,623 --> 00:14:00,206
but Rasool Allah ﷺ treated them that way as Bil-Misl(بالمثل) equally as they have treated the shepherd of Rasool Allah ﷺ

180
00:14:00,271 --> 00:14:05,168
and we know that in Islam, if 100 people gathered together, to kill one person

181
00:14:05,454 --> 00:14:10,924
then all of them are subjected to the Qisaas(قصاص), the retribution.

182
00:14:11,318 --> 00:14:12,504
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) says;

183
00:14:13,061 --> 00:14:17,140
If the residents of San'a(صنعاء) come together to kill one man

184
00:14:17,382 --> 00:14:20,246
then all of them will be executed for that

185
00:14:20,270 --> 00:14:23,645
this is the Hukm(حكم) of Sharia(شريعة) in Hudood(حدود).

186
00:14:24,587 --> 00:14:28,233
So, these are some comments on this Hadith(حديث) in Bukhari(بخاري),

187
00:14:28,550 --> 00:14:35,238
and as Ibn Kathir(اِبْنِ كَثِيْر) mentioned, it occurred within the period of the sixth year of Hijrah(هجرة).

188
00:14:35,536 --> 00:14:38,577
Some other events that occurred during that year,

189
00:14:38,774 --> 00:14:41,105
these are small Saraya(سرلية), dispatches.

190
00:14:41,461 --> 00:14:45,751
In Rabiul Awwal(ربيع اول) of that year Rasool Allah ﷺ sent or Ukkasha Bin Mahsan(عكاشة بن محصن)

191
00:14:46,034 --> 00:14:48,694
with a force of 40 men to Ghamar Marzooq(غَمَرمَرْزُوْق)

192
00:14:49,099 --> 00:14:53,084
the enemy fled from him and he encamped at their wells.

193
00:14:53,522 --> 00:14:59,053
He then sent some men in pursuit of them and took 200 of their camels which, he led to Madina.

194
00:14:59,093 --> 00:15:00,665
 These were taken as Ghaneemah(غنيمه).

195
00:15:00,950 --> 00:15:05,437
Also that year, was the dispatch of Abu Obaidah(أبوعبيدة) to Zul-Qissah(ذوالقصه)

196
00:15:05,713 --> 00:15:09,152
he had with him 40 men, he made for them on foot

197
00:15:09,500 --> 00:15:12,069
reaching them in the morning, while it was still dark.

198
00:15:12,564 --> 00:15:15,268
They fled from him into the mountain heights

199
00:15:15,603 --> 00:15:18,929
he captured one of their men and brought into the Messenger of Allah.

200
00:15:19,762 --> 00:15:23,815
And then there was the dispatch of Muhammad Ibn Maslamah(محمدإبن مسلمه) with the force of 10 men,

201
00:15:24,092 --> 00:15:26,562
the enemy hide from him until night

202
00:15:27,503 --> 00:15:31,051
and then all of the men of Muhammad Ibn Maslamah(محمدإبن مسلمه) were killed

203
00:15:31,376 --> 00:15:34,072
except he escaped but he was wounded.

204
00:15:34,498 --> 00:15:38,462
Al-Yamdo'al(أليمدولِم), One day you win the next day you lose

205
00:15:38,502 --> 00:15:41,418
 that's the Sunnah(سنة) of Allahعَزّوجَلّ in Duniyah(دُنِيَّا).

206
00:15:41,785 --> 00:15:47,140
So, one cannot stop, the struggle just because of suffering a setback.

207
00:15:47,808 --> 00:15:52,275
Muhammad Ibn Maslamah(محمدإبن مسلمه) was the only one from this group who escaped alive.

208
00:15:52,662 --> 00:15:56,655
And then Rasool Allah ﷺ sent Zaid Bin Harissa(زيدبن حارثة) to Al-Jamoom(ألجموم)

209
00:15:57,128 --> 00:15:59,866
he also sent Zaid Bin Harissa(زيدبن حارثه) to Bannu Thalabah(بنو ثعلبة).

210
00:16:00,081 --> 00:16:02,346
He sends Zaid Bin Harissa(زيدبن حارثه) to Al-Ees(ألعيص).

211
00:16:02,872 --> 00:16:10,798
Here we see Zaid Bin Harissa رضي الله عنه sent to lead three Sarayah(سرايه) within one year

212
00:16:11,482 --> 00:16:17,583
and this shows us the level of the trust that Rasool Allah ﷺ has in Zaid Bin Harissa(زيدبن حارثه)

213
00:16:18,116 --> 00:16:21,585
who was his former slave and Rasool Allah ﷺ, freed him

214
00:16:21,999 --> 00:16:24,817
and then Rasool Allah ﷺ married him, to a woman

215
00:16:25,161 --> 00:16:29,607
that the belongs the nobility of Makkah, Zainab Bint Jahash رضي الله عنها

216
00:16:29,631 --> 00:16:30,750
we talked about her story.

217
00:16:31,012 --> 00:16:35,235
And this shows us again the trust that Rasool Allah ﷺ had, in Zaid Bin Harissa(زيدبن حارثه)

218
00:16:35,529 --> 00:16:41,134
a man who without Islam would never imagine in his life that he would lead an army,

219
00:16:41,518 --> 00:16:46,506
he wouldn't even imagine that he would be a free man honored in the society,

220
00:16:46,531 --> 00:16:54,445
let alone, lead an army that had some of the great men of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) or Al-Khazraj(ألخزرج) or Al-Aos(ألأوس).

221
00:16:54,922 --> 00:17:01,050
And then Rasool Allah ﷺ would appoint him, sometime later as, we will talk about to lead,

222
00:17:01,347 --> 00:17:05,982
in one of the great battles of Islamic history Ghazwa Mo'ta(غزوة مؤته).

223
00:17:06,923 --> 00:17:10,624
Only to be honored by Allahعَزّوجَلّ and die as a Shaheed(شهيد).

224
00:17:11,043 --> 00:17:16,344
Rasool Allah ﷺ sent Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) to Banni Saeed Bin Bakr(بني سعيد بن بكر) and they were sent,

225
00:17:16,424 --> 00:17:23,633
because Rasool Allah ﷺ heard that, these people were planning on giving the Jews of Al-Khaybar(الخيبر) some assistance.

226
00:17:24,069 --> 00:17:27,728
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ wanted to prevent that.

227
00:17:28,093 --> 00:17:31,656
And he sent Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) to them they did not fight,

228
00:17:32,029 --> 00:17:36,076
they fled from Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) he captured one of their men,

229
00:17:36,332 --> 00:17:42,698
and this man admitted to being a spy for them and they retrieve some information from him.

230
00:17:43,190 --> 00:17:45,764
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ, you can see from the story

231
00:17:46,151 --> 00:17:49,570
that he was very aware of what was happening around him

232
00:17:50,051 --> 00:17:56,191
he had very strong intelligence of everything that was going on, in Arabia.

233
00:17:56,664 --> 00:18:02,322
He had for example Khuza'a(خزاعه), acting as intelligence officers for him

234
00:18:02,501 --> 00:18:04,462
getting information from Quraish(قريش)

235
00:18:04,794 --> 00:18:09,287
he had information from the areas in which the Jews were living,

236
00:18:09,720 --> 00:18:15,270
he had intelligence coming to him for what was happening in Ghatafaan(غطافان),

237
00:18:15,553 --> 00:18:21,877
Rasool Allah ﷺ was not taken by surprise, in fact, he would take his enemies by surprise.

238
00:18:22,765 --> 00:18:27,764
Rasool Allah ﷺ we can see that, not only were the Muslim strong in the battlefield

239
00:18:28,034 --> 00:18:30,934
but they were very strong in reconnaissance, and gathering information.

240
00:18:31,359 --> 00:18:34,771
Abdur Rahman Ibn Auf رضي الله عنه was sent to Doma-Tul-Jandal(دومة الجندل).

241
00:18:34,977 --> 00:18:39,634
And the instructions were to go and give them Da'wah(دعوة) to Islam, if they accept Islam

242
00:18:39,915 --> 00:18:43,303
then offer to marry the daughter of their king.

243
00:18:43,752 --> 00:18:49,752
And that did happen and Abdur Rahman Ibn Auf(عبدالرحمن ابن عوف) married the daughter of their king Al-Asbigh Al-Kalbi(اَلْاَصْبَغْ اَلْكَلْبِيْ).

244
00:18:49,965 --> 00:18:56,696
Her name was Tumadhir(تُمَاضِر) and she was married to Abdur Rahman Ibn Auf رضي الله عنه.

245
00:18:57,230 --> 00:18:59,032
These are some scattered events that occurred in the six year of Hijrah(هجرة).

246
00:18:59,057 --> 00:19:03,800


247
00:19:03,824 --> 00:19:10,288
We move on to the seven year, now Rasool Allah ﷺ came back from Al-Hudaybiyya(اَلْحُدَيْبِيَة)

248
00:19:10,924 --> 00:19:11,986
Musa Bin Uqba(موسى بن عقبه)

249
00:19:12,178 --> 00:19:15,875
 and by the way, Musa Bin Uqba(موسى بن عُقْبَه) is an author of Seerah(سيرة)

250
00:19:16,559 --> 00:19:22,402
and the scholars say that his narrations are among the best

251
00:19:23,320 --> 00:19:26,281
when it comes to the Seerah(سيرة) of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

252
00:19:26,433 --> 00:19:30,350
However, the book that he authored does not exist with us today.

253
00:19:30,799 --> 00:19:35,832
What exists with us today are narrations from him by other scholars.

254
00:19:36,602 --> 00:19:43,299
So, other scholars like a Ibn Is'haqq(اِبْنِ اِسْحَاقْ) like Al-Waqidie(ألواقعدي) they would narrate from Musa Bin Uqba(موسى بن عُقْبَه).

255
00:19:43,852 --> 00:19:45,574
Musa Bin Uqba(موسى بن عُقْبَه) says that,

256
00:19:45,860 --> 00:19:54,309
20 days after the arrival of Rasool Allah ﷺ to Madina from Al-Hudaybiyya(اَلْحُدَيْبِيَّة), he set out to Khaybar(خيبر).

257
00:19:55,022 --> 00:20:00,336
Now Al-Hudaybiyya(اَلْحُدَيْبِيَّة) was a truce, between Rasool Allah ﷺ and Quraish(قُرَيْشْ)

258
00:20:00,864 --> 00:20:04,296
and the agreement was that, they would stop fighting for 10 years.

259
00:20:05,005 --> 00:20:12,360
Now, rather than the Muslims taking rest from a very difficult five years

260
00:20:12,959 --> 00:20:17,673
of continuous fighting with Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) and the allies of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ).

261
00:20:18,063 --> 00:20:19,888
No, they did not take rest,

262
00:20:20,539 --> 00:20:27,540
only 20 days after the arrival in Madina Rasool Allah ﷺ is marching out to Khaybar(خيبر).

263
00:20:28,038 --> 00:20:34,735
Rasool Allah ﷺ has now, a peace agreement with Quraish(قُرَيْشْ)

264
00:20:35,441 --> 00:20:38,310
but there's the big problem of Al-Yahood(إليهود)

265
00:20:39,034 --> 00:20:42,534
who were continuously conspiring against the Muslims.

266
00:20:43,282 --> 00:20:47,452
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ saw this as the appropriate moment

267
00:20:48,132 --> 00:20:55,934
to once and for all stop the Yahood(إليهود) from their conspiracies against the Muslims.

268
00:20:56,396 --> 00:21:00,557
And the only remaining stronghold of Al-Yahood(إليهود).

269
00:21:00,628 --> 00:21:03,406
There is still another community of Yahood(إليهود) in Tayma(تيماء)

270
00:21:03,470 --> 00:21:08,537
but this was the only remaining stronghold of Al-Yahood(إليهود)  and this was Khaybar(خيبر).

271
00:21:08,775 --> 00:21:13,140
In fact it was the strongest area of Al-Yahood(إليهود) in the Arabian Peninsula.

272
00:21:13,628 --> 00:21:21,244
On the way Amir Bin Aqwa رضي الله عنه was asked to make Nasheed(نشيد) for them,

273
00:21:21,640 --> 00:21:26,826
the Bedouin way of singing poetry and this is Huda'a(هداء).

274
00:21:27,136 --> 00:21:32,365
And Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله) this had an effect on the camels,

275
00:21:32,730 --> 00:21:39,497
the camels would become active and faster and stronger in their march if they become tired,

276
00:21:39,760 --> 00:21:42,167
when they hear these Anasheed(اَنَاشِيْد).

277
00:21:42,499 --> 00:21:46,254
So, Aamir(عامر) was told to make this Nasheed(نشيد) and he said;

278
00:21:46,594 --> 00:21:50,683
Allah humma(اَللَّهُمَّ) without you we would not have been rightly guided***

279
00:21:50,929 --> 00:21:54,095
Nor would we have given alms nor prayed***

280
00:21:54,490 --> 00:21:58,097
We beseech you, to forgive what, we have done wrong***

281
00:21:58,476 --> 00:22:00,732
May we be sacrificed for you***

282
00:22:00,955 --> 00:22:04,272
We beseech you to send down, your serenity upon us***

283
00:22:04,612 --> 00:22:07,945
To make our feet secure, when we meet our enemies***

284
00:22:08,332 --> 00:22:11,237
And if they cry out trying to subvert us***

285
00:22:11,269 --> 00:22:16,646
We will refuse already have the loudly sought others, help against us***

286
00:22:17,190 --> 00:22:23,272
When Rasool Allah ﷺ heard these wonderful words from Amir Bin Aqwa(عامربن اكوع)

287
00:22:23,587 --> 00:22:28,588
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: Yarhamo Hullah(يرحمهُ الله), may Allah have mercy on him.

288
00:22:28,920 --> 00:22:36,262
And the Sahabah(صحابه) knew that when Rasool Allah ﷺ singles out an individual for mercy

289
00:22:36,286 --> 00:22:38,139
that means, he will die as Shaheed(شهيد),

290
00:22:38,964 --> 00:22:41,207
Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله) that's the understanding they had

291
00:22:41,797 --> 00:22:45,230
as if Shahadah(شهادة) and mercy are related.

292
00:22:45,546 --> 00:22:49,692
So when Rasool Allah ﷺ would say Yarhamo Hullah(يرحمهُ الله) may Allah have mercy on him.

293
00:22:49,894 --> 00:22:51,658
When Rasool Allah ﷺ make that Dua(دعا)

294
00:22:51,724 --> 00:22:53,999
the manifestation of this Dua(دُعَا)

295
00:22:54,023 --> 00:22:56,467
would come in the form of Shahadah(شهادة) in the form of martyrdom.

296
00:22:56,865 --> 00:22:58,439
So Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) said;

297
00:22:58,842 --> 00:23:00,096
وَجَبَتْ يا رسول الله,

298
00:23:00,556 --> 00:23:02,201
It has become inevitable.

299
00:23:02,612 --> 00:23:03,688
لَوْلَا مَتعتنا بِه

300
00:23:03,712 --> 00:23:07,210
I wish you have allowed us to enjoy his company longer,

301
00:23:07,636 --> 00:23:11,030
so they're not protesting that Aamir(عامر) would become a shaheed(شهيد).

302
00:23:11,088 --> 00:23:15,343
They're happy for him that he would receive this blessing from Allahعَزّوجَلّ

303
00:23:15,691 --> 00:23:21,763
but they just wanted to enjoy him longer because, they enjoy his company

304
00:23:22,354 --> 00:23:25,520
and they would have desired that, they would have spent more time with him.

305
00:23:26,118 --> 00:23:32,795
The Muslims reached to Khaybar(خيبر), the Yahood(يهود) of Khaybar(خيبر) as we said;

306
00:23:32,898 --> 00:23:36,693
Rasool Allah ﷺ has taken his enemies by surprise,

307
00:23:36,970 --> 00:23:42,107
they set out in the morning to go out of their fortresses into their farms,

308
00:23:42,626 --> 00:23:47,041
so they came out with their equipment farming equipment, ready for work

309
00:23:47,374 --> 00:23:51,129
and they suddenly see, the army in the horizon.

310
00:23:51,234 --> 00:23:53,897
They run back into their fortresses saying;

311
00:23:53,989 --> 00:23:57,176
محمد وَالْخَمِيْسْ، محمد وَالْخَمِيْسْ، محمد وَالْخَمِيْسْ،

312
00:23:57,587 --> 00:24:01,347
Muhammad Wal Khamees(محمد والخميس) Al-Khamees(الخميس) means, the army, Muhammad(محمد) and the army,

313
00:24:01,372 --> 00:24:05,626
Muhammad(محمد) and the army, Muhammad(محمد) and the army, these were their words

314
00:24:05,876 --> 00:24:09,689
when they're fleeing and running away from Muhammadﷺ.

315
00:24:10,505 --> 00:24:12,179
Now, these Yahood(يهود) they used to brag,

316
00:24:12,219 --> 00:24:18,281
the Yahood(يهود) of Khaybar(خيبر), they used to brag and say that fighting us, is not like fighting the rest of the Arabs and

317
00:24:18,576 --> 00:24:25,435
they were proud and happy and content with their fortresses and their, strong training

318
00:24:25,812 --> 00:24:29,857
and the famous fighting men among them, such as Marhab(مرحب), and others.

319
00:24:30,305 --> 00:24:35,173
But when they saw, the army of Muhammadﷺ, they fled and ran away

320
00:24:35,598 --> 00:24:37,926
and this is because Rasool Allah ﷺ says;

321
00:24:37,951 --> 00:24:40,011
نُصِرْتُ بِرُّعْبَ مسيْرَةْ الشَّهْرْ

322
00:24:40,421 --> 00:24:42,513
I was given victory through fear,

323
00:24:42,752 --> 00:24:46,768
Allahعَزّوجَلّ puts fear in the hearts of the enemies of Muhammadﷺ.

324
00:24:47,591 --> 00:24:53,425
When Rasool Allah ﷺ laid siege to the fortresses of Khaybar(خيبر)

325
00:24:53,450 --> 00:25:00,734
we're not talking about one fortress but many fortresses scattered around on hill tops and mountains, very well protected area.

326
00:25:01,267 --> 00:25:09,374
The news spread and the Arabs knew very well, the strength of the location,

327
00:25:09,925 --> 00:25:13,406
and strength of Al-Yahood(إليهود) in that area.

328
00:25:14,263 --> 00:25:19,853
And Huwaitib Ibn Abdul Izzah(حويطب إبن عبدالعزة) who was one of the members of the envoys

329
00:25:20,153 --> 00:25:22,824
who met with Rasool Allah ﷺ in Hudaybiyya(حُدَيْبِية).

330
00:25:23,407 --> 00:25:25,616
When he went back to Makkah, he said;

331
00:25:25,958 --> 00:25:29,727
He's narrating this, he said: When I left from Al-Hudaybiyya(الْحُدَيْبِيَة),

332
00:25:30,067 --> 00:25:33,982
I knew that Muhammad(محمد) and his followers would be victorious.

333
00:25:34,352 --> 00:25:36,620
This is the impression of the people,

334
00:25:36,969 --> 00:25:42,531
people when they would come and meet with Rasool Allah ﷺ and see him, and hear him

335
00:25:42,794 --> 00:25:45,326
and they would see, the conduct of the Muslims,

336
00:25:45,971 --> 00:25:50,178
they would carry a certain impression, as we see with Urwa Bin Masood(عُرْوَة بن مسعود),

337
00:25:50,218 --> 00:25:56,029
 the impression, he had is that the way, Rasool Allah ﷺ is treated by his followers

338
00:25:56,321 --> 00:25:59,908
 is like no other in the world, it is unique

339
00:26:00,224 --> 00:26:06,519
and he also came back with the impression that his followers are never going to give them up, no matter what happens.

340
00:26:06,719 --> 00:26:10,463
Huwaitib Ibn Abdul Uzzah(حويطب إبن عبدالعزة), he came back with the impression that

341
00:26:10,487 --> 00:26:13,354
these people are going to definitely win.

342
00:26:14,366 --> 00:26:18,276
So, he and some other men from Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) had a bet.

343
00:26:18,842 --> 00:26:24,014
Some of them people of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) like the Safwan Ibn Umayyah(صفوان ابن اُمَيَّة) they were for Al-Yahood(إليهود),

344
00:26:24,054 --> 00:26:25,575
they said that Yahood(إليهود) will win

345
00:26:25,938 --> 00:26:27,869
because of the reputation that they had.

346
00:26:28,497 --> 00:26:34,478
While Huwaitib(حويطب) said Muhammadﷺ will win and the wager was 100 camels

347
00:26:34,721 --> 00:26:36,419
that was the bet, a hundred camels.

348
00:26:36,954 --> 00:26:44,260
So, the news has spread and it has gained the interest of people all over

349
00:26:44,545 --> 00:26:47,055
to the extent that they would have a bet about it, in Makkah.

350
00:26:47,785 --> 00:26:51,210
During the siege of one of the fortresses,

351
00:26:51,496 --> 00:27:01,561
one of the fighters of Al-Yahood(إليهود), I think it's Marhab(مَرْحَب) he came out asking for a duel challenging the Muslims.

352
00:27:01,691 --> 00:27:06,347
 So, Aamir Ibn Al Aqwa(عامر ابن الاكوع) is the one who came out to meet him.

353
00:27:06,669 --> 00:27:09,655
They exchanged a few blows with their swords

354
00:27:10,090 --> 00:27:15,751
and then Marhab(مَرْحَب), he struck Aamir(عامر) with his sword

355
00:27:16,053 --> 00:27:22,778
but the sword got stuck in the shield that, Aamir(عامر) had, it was leather or wood,

356
00:27:22,954 --> 00:27:28,513
so it withheld his sword in it, and Marhab(مَرْحَب) was unable to pull it out.

357
00:27:29,001 --> 00:27:34,769
So Aamir(عامر) took this as an opportunity to strike at Marhab(مَرْحَب) and kill him

358
00:27:35,099 --> 00:27:42,401
but, his sword was short, so it came back on him and it struck, the upper part of his knee

359
00:27:42,882 --> 00:27:48,556
and it hit an artery or vein and Aamir(عامر) bled to death and he died.

360
00:27:49,165 --> 00:27:54,942
So now some people started saying that Aamir(عامر) has lost all of his deeds

361
00:27:54,982 --> 00:27:56,499
because he has committed suicide.

362
00:27:57,362 --> 00:28:02,520
Salamah(سلمة), who is his nephew, was very upset with that,

363
00:28:02,560 --> 00:28:04,627
 and depressed with what people were saying

364
00:28:05,295 --> 00:28:09,309
and Rasool Allah ﷺ saw that on his face, so he asked him; What's wrong with you?

365
00:28:09,349 --> 00:28:10,115
He said;

366
00:28:10,466 --> 00:28:13,313
People are claiming that my uncle Aamir(عامر).

367
00:28:13,337 --> 00:28:14,329
بَطُلَ عَمَلُه

368
00:28:14,353 --> 00:28:16,323
That he lost all of his deeds.

369
00:28:17,015 --> 00:28:20,777
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: Kadhaboo(كذبو), whoever said that, lied.

370
00:28:21,339 --> 00:28:28,406
He will receive a double reward and then he raised, both of his fingers to signify double the reward.

371
00:28:28,801 --> 00:28:34,787
He was a Mujahid(مجاهد), who struggled his best, and a few Arabs have matched him,

372
00:28:35,264 --> 00:28:40,650
اِنَّه’ جَاهِدٌ مُجَاهِدْ قَلَّمَا مَشى عَرَبِيٌّ مِثْلُ

373
00:28:41,372 --> 00:28:48,942
So, this is a badge of honor that, Amir Bin Aqwa رضي الله عنه received from Rasool Allah ﷺ

374
00:28:49,105 --> 00:28:53,681
and what we just talked about earlier, the Dua(دُعَا) of Rasool Allah ﷺ happened.

375
00:28:53,705 --> 00:28:55,997
When Rasool Allah ﷺ said: Yahamo Hullah(يرحمه الله)

376
00:28:56,137 --> 00:28:59,562
the Dua(دُعَا) was accepted then it was accepted very soon.

377
00:28:59,832 --> 00:29:03,391
He was killed in the same battle, Ghazwat-Khaybar(غزوة الخيبر).

378
00:29:03,918 --> 00:29:07,225
There was a particular fortress that was giving the Muslims hard time

379
00:29:07,833 --> 00:29:13,830
one after another Rasool Allah ﷺ would appoint leaders to open it and they would all failed.

380
00:29:14,498 --> 00:29:16,913
And then Rasool Allah ﷺ, one evening said;

381
00:29:17,026 --> 00:29:26,701
لَاُعطيَّنَّ الرَاية غَدًا رَجُلًا يَفْتَحُ الله َعَلَى يَدَيْهِ يُحِبُ اللهَ وَرَسُوْلَه، وَيُحِبُّهُ اللهُ وَرَسُوْلَهْ

382
00:29:27,190 --> 00:29:33,346
Tomorrow, I will give the banner to a man, whom Allah will open for him.

383
00:29:33,709 --> 00:29:39,221
He loves Allah and His messenger, and Allah and His Messenger love him.

384
00:29:39,245 --> 00:29:45,133
What a wonderful honor, Allah will open this fortress for him,

385
00:29:45,388 --> 00:29:49,236
he loves Allah and His messenger and Allah and His Messenger love him.

386
00:29:49,701 --> 00:29:50,915
Sahal Ibn Sa'ad(سهل إبن سعد) said;

387
00:29:50,939 --> 00:29:55,534
فَلَمَّا اَصْبَحَ النَّاسْ غَدَّوْا عَلَى النَّبِيْ كُلَّهُمْ يَرْجُوْ اَنْ يُعْطَاهَا

388
00:29:56,788 --> 00:30:02,458
Next day, in the morning all of the Sahabah(صحابه) went to Rasool Allah ﷺ

389
00:30:02,712 --> 00:30:07,141
showing themselves, in front of him, to turns his attention towards them

390
00:30:07,511 --> 00:30:10,913
because everyone of them, wanted that honor, for himself.

391
00:30:10,953 --> 00:30:12,072
And this is in Al-Bukhari(إلبخاري).

392
00:30:12,706 --> 00:30:15,930
And I want you, to pay attention to this statement, by Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب)

393
00:30:16,676 --> 00:30:18,818
it's a striking statement. He said;

394
00:30:19,111 --> 00:30:22,979
فَمَا اَحْبَبْتُ الْاِمَارَة قَطْ اِلَّا يَوْمَئِذٍ

395
00:30:23,978 --> 00:30:24,885
And this is in Al-Muslim(المسلم).

396
00:30:24,909 --> 00:30:32,074
He said: I never loved position of authority ever, except on that day

397
00:30:32,808 --> 00:30:39,673
loving, to be an Ameer(اَمِيْر), loving to be in a position of authority, is something that everyone has

398
00:30:40,536 --> 00:30:46,551
the love of being famous, the love of being known, the love of being an authority the love of being in power,

399
00:30:46,781 --> 00:30:50,041
this is something natural to humans.

400
00:30:50,495 --> 00:30:52,217
However, in Islam,

401
00:30:52,487 --> 00:30:58,222
we are not supposed to seek for positions of authority to be dominant over others to give orders.

402
00:30:58,562 --> 00:31:00,321
That is something that is discouraged,

403
00:31:00,824 --> 00:31:06,055
when Al-Abbas(العباس) came to Rasool Allah ﷺ, asking him being the uncle of Rasool Ullah

404
00:31:06,535 --> 00:31:11,177
asking him to appoint him in a position of authority, Rasool Allah ﷺ told him;

405
00:31:11,210 --> 00:31:14,739
اِنَّ لَا نُعْطِعْي هَذَالْاَمْرَ اَحَدًا سَئلَهُ اَو حَرَص عَلَيْهْ

406
00:31:15,031 --> 00:31:20,118
We do not give this, to somebody who asks for it, or somebody who's eager to have it.

407
00:31:20,965 --> 00:31:24,832
This is the Tarbiyyah(تربيعة) of Rasool Allah ﷺ, this is the Tarbiyyah(تربيعة) of Islam.

408
00:31:25,429 --> 00:31:30,171
And it reached to the level that Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) doesn't even desire it.

409
00:31:30,434 --> 00:31:34,437
So, it's not like he's suppressing his desire for it, he doesn't want it

410
00:31:34,758 --> 00:31:40,765
he has reached to the level, where he was able to force himself into not even wanting it

411
00:31:41,277 --> 00:31:51,449
and it moved on, from that level of suppressing this desire into the level of genuinely not seeking it, and not loving it,

412
00:31:51,726 --> 00:31:53,930
except that day, he wanted it, why?

413
00:31:53,970 --> 00:31:56,908
Because of the honor and the promise of most of Rasool Allah ﷺ that

414
00:31:56,932 --> 00:32:00,242
this is a man that loves Allah, and His Messenger and Allah and His Messenger love him.

415
00:32:00,808 --> 00:32:03,355
This is something that every Sahabi(صحابي) wanted to have.

416
00:32:04,343 --> 00:32:09,843
So, brothers and sisters, this is an opportunity for us to remind ourselves

417
00:32:10,426 --> 00:32:15,294
on this danger of Hubb-Al-Ammarah(حب الأمارة) of Love of leadership.

418
00:32:15,814 --> 00:32:21,055
Rasool Allah ﷺ says, in a Hadith(حديث) narrated by Tirmizi(تِرْمِذِي) and it is Hasan Sahih(حسن صحيح).

419
00:32:21,282 --> 00:32:28,062
مَا ذئْبَانِ جَائعان اُرْسِلَا فِيْ غَنَمْ بِاَفْسَدَلَهَا مِنْ حرص المرء عَلَى الْمَالِ والَشَّرفْ لِدِيْنِه

420
00:32:28,184 --> 00:32:36,706
If you sent two hungry wolves, on some sheep they will not corrupt the sheep more than,

421
00:32:36,956 --> 00:32:45,876
 the eagerness that the person has for wealth and position of authority, for his religion.

422
00:32:47,172 --> 00:32:53,694
So, the meaning of this Hadith(حديث) is, that if a person has the love and eagerness to have money,

423
00:32:53,930 --> 00:33:01,003
 and to have authority, these two things are dangerous on his religion,

424
00:33:01,527 --> 00:33:08,644
just like the danger of sending two hungry wolves on sheep.

425
00:33:09,082 --> 00:33:12,306
Now, if you sent to hungry wolves and sheep, what could they do?

426
00:33:12,353 --> 00:33:13,496
They would ruin them.

427
00:33:13,714 --> 00:33:16,235
And the same thing, would happen to your religion

428
00:33:16,692 --> 00:33:21,240
if you allow the love of money and the love of authority to take over.

429
00:33:21,900 --> 00:33:26,272
So, these are two things, that we have to make Mujahidah(مجاهده) against we have to struggle against.

430
00:33:26,709 --> 00:33:28,164
 And it's a continuous struggle

431
00:33:28,636 --> 00:33:31,667
it's not something that you do for a while and then you Leave

432
00:33:31,691 --> 00:33:34,858
it's a continuous struggle that we have with our Nafs(نفس),

433
00:33:35,239 --> 00:33:36,369
and in Al-Bukhari(ألبخاري).

434
00:33:36,393 --> 00:33:40,426
اِنَّكُمْ سَتَحْرِصُوْنَ عَلَى الْاِمَارَةَ وَ اِنَّهَا ندَامَة يَوْمَ الْقِيَامَةْ

435
00:33:41,057 --> 00:33:48,035
You will have, love of authority and you will regret it on the Day of Judgment.

436
00:33:48,516 --> 00:33:51,502
It will be regret on the Day of Judgment.

437
00:33:51,527 --> 00:33:54,575
So, we need to be careful brothers and sisters, we need to be very careful.

438
00:33:55,118 --> 00:33:59,028
Whom did Rasool Allah ﷺ then give Rayi'ah(راية), whom did he give, the banner to?

439
00:33:59,626 --> 00:34:03,493
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: Where is Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب)?

440
00:34:03,779 --> 00:34:04,262
They told him;

441
00:34:04,286 --> 00:34:05,748
اِنَّهُ اَرْمَدْ يَا رَسُول الله

442
00:34:06,057 --> 00:34:09,622
They told him that he's suffering the disease in his eyes.

443
00:34:10,376 --> 00:34:14,442
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: Bring him, so they brought him, his eyes were shut,

444
00:34:14,906 --> 00:34:18,763
so they had to hold him by the hand and bring him to the Rasool Allah ﷺ.

445
00:34:19,050 --> 00:34:25,625
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ put some of this saliva in the eyes of Allah Bin Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) and they were immediately cured.

446
00:34:26,685 --> 00:34:32,826
This is one of the miracles of Rasool Allah ﷺ, one of the many miracles of Rasool Allah ﷺ

447
00:34:33,521 --> 00:34:38,917
and then Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) was handed the banner and he told Rasool Allah ﷺ.

448
00:34:38,942 --> 00:34:41,865
اُقَاتِلُهُمْ يَا رَسُوْلْ الله حَتَّى يَكُوْنُوْا مِثْلَنَا

449
00:34:41,889 --> 00:34:44,868
Should I fight them until, they become like us.

450
00:34:45,162 --> 00:34:49,870
 And this is interesting Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) didn't say Should I fight them, until they become Muslim.

451
00:34:49,894 --> 00:34:50,670
What did he say?

452
00:34:50,900 --> 00:34:53,124
He said: Should, I fight them until they become like us.

453
00:34:53,484 --> 00:34:58,170
So, they were the living example of Islam, they and Islam were synonymous.

454
00:34:59,417 --> 00:35:02,466
So, whether he said, shall I fight them until they become Muslim

455
00:35:02,490 --> 00:35:05,719
or shall I fight them until they become like us, doesn't make a difference,

456
00:35:05,743 --> 00:35:06,629
they mean the same thing.

457
00:35:07,172 --> 00:35:10,103
something that we cannot say today, something we cannot claim today.

458
00:35:10,850 --> 00:35:12,515
Rasool Allah ﷺ told him;

459
00:35:12,801 --> 00:35:14,306
اِنْفِذ عَلَى رِسْلِكْ

460
00:35:14,474 --> 00:35:18,360
حَتَّى تَنْزِلَ بِسَاحَتِهِمْ ثُمَّ ادْعُهُمْ اِلَىْ الْاِسْلَامْ

461
00:35:18,384 --> 00:35:22,236
ووَاَخْبِرْهُمْ بِمَا يَجِبُ عَلَيْهِمْ مِنْ حَقِّ الله تَعَالى

462
00:35:22,584 --> 00:35:29,660
من حَقِّ الله تَعَالى فِيْه، فَوَلله لَا اَنْ يَّهْدِيَ الله بِكَ رَجُلًا وَاحِدَا خَيْرُ الَّكَ مِنْ خُمْرً نَّعْمْ

463
00:35:30,214 --> 00:35:32,899
In Bukhari(بخاريْ) Rasool Allah ﷺ told him;

464
00:35:33,176 --> 00:35:36,007
Go to them, until you reach

465
00:35:36,524 --> 00:35:37,395
بِسَاحَتهِمْ

466
00:35:37,474 --> 00:35:41,998
the area in front of them, and then invite them to Islam

467
00:35:42,354 --> 00:35:46,343
and inform them about their duties towards Allah

468
00:35:47,057 --> 00:35:48,517
and then Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

469
00:35:48,723 --> 00:35:55,769
In the name of Allah, if Allah guides through you , one man, it's better for you than, the best of camels.

470
00:35:56,711 --> 00:36:00,415
Here is an example of Ghaneemah(غنيمة) and guidance

471
00:36:00,440 --> 00:36:04,486
if Allah guides one man through you, it's better for you than Ghaneemah(غنيمة)

472
00:36:04,510 --> 00:36:06,530
it's better for you than the greatest Ghaneemah(غنيمة).

473
00:36:07,266 --> 00:36:11,535
And this, points out to us the purpose of Jihad(جهاد) Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله).

474
00:36:12,624 --> 00:36:19,625
The paramount, the most important goal of Jihad(جهاد) Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله)

475
00:36:19,650 --> 00:36:26,383
is to spread the truth, it is to invite others to Islam, it is to save them from hellfire, it is to benefit them

476
00:36:27,063 --> 00:36:32,848
with the greatest benefit, it is to provide them with the best thing and, that is Islam.

477
00:36:33,633 --> 00:36:39,063
And this is, what makes war in a Islam completely different, than any other type of war

478
00:36:39,087 --> 00:36:40,898
any other war, that happens in the world.

479
00:36:41,862 --> 00:36:49,175
Other wars are fought for booty, they are fought for hunger, for power,

480
00:36:49,437 --> 00:36:54,453
they are fought for revenge, they are fought for different reasons.

481
00:36:54,981 --> 00:37:00,793
But here we see the noble, idea of fighting, in order to save people

482
00:37:01,531 --> 00:37:03,449
and that's why Rasool Allah ﷺ says;

483
00:37:03,672 --> 00:37:07,867
I am amazed, by people who are dragged into paradise in chains.

484
00:37:08,809 --> 00:37:13,136
Meaning people sometimes, are forced into Jannah(جنة) against their will.

485
00:37:13,398 --> 00:37:16,975
And this because, they were fought and then they became Muslim

486
00:37:17,425 --> 00:37:21,504
and Rasool Allah ﷺ, is turning the attention of Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب)

487
00:37:21,528 --> 00:37:25,143
that you should first, give them Da'wah(دعوة), before fighting them.

488
00:37:25,786 --> 00:37:30,493
And that if one man becomes Muslim, that's better for you than the best of Ghaneemah(غنيمة).

489
00:37:31,692 --> 00:37:35,166
The slogan of the Muslims in that battle

490
00:37:35,198 --> 00:37:39,546
they used to have different slogans in different battles, in this particular battle, it was;

491
00:37:39,574 --> 00:37:41,417
يَامَنْصُوْرَ أَمِتْ أَمِتْ

492
00:37:41,819 --> 00:37:45,934
O, Victor, kill, kill or put to death, put to death.

493
00:37:45,974 --> 00:37:48,874
And this is something that they would repeat.

494
00:37:49,329 --> 00:37:51,964
Ibn Is'haqq(اِبْنِ اِسْحَاقْ) says that Salamah(سلمة) narrated

495
00:37:52,429 --> 00:37:57,688
that Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) carried the banner and walked to them with confidence

496
00:37:58,265 --> 00:38:03,850
and we are following him until, he reached next to their fortress

497
00:38:04,308 --> 00:38:11,613
and posted the banner, in a pile of rocks, under the fortress.

498
00:38:12,117 --> 00:38:16,694
So, a Jew looked to Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب), from on top of the fortress

499
00:38:16,719 --> 00:38:20,031
he looked down at Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) from top of the fortress and said;

500
00:38:20,055 --> 00:38:20,873
Who are you?

501
00:38:21,347 --> 00:38:23,751
قَالَ  اَنَا عَلِيْ بن ابي طالب

502
00:38:24,122 --> 00:38:27,588
I am Ali(علي), the son of Abu Talib(ابو طالب).

503
00:38:27,825 --> 00:38:28,460
The Jew said;

504
00:38:28,485 --> 00:38:30,789
تعَالَيْتُمْ وَمَا اُنزِلَ على مُوسى

505
00:38:31,228 --> 00:38:35,596
You will rise in the name of, what has been revealed on Musa(موسى).

506
00:38:35,732 --> 00:38:37,193
Because the name of Ali(علي),

507
00:38:37,486 --> 00:38:41,263
Ali(علي) is from Al'luww(عَلُوّْ) and that is something that is high and exalted.

508
00:38:41,837 --> 00:38:47,483
So, when this Yahoodi(يهودي) heard the name of Ali(علي) he said, that you will rise.

509
00:38:47,508 --> 00:38:51,249
He took it as a bad omen because of the name of Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب)

510
00:38:51,289 --> 00:38:56,492
 it means Al'luww(عَلُوّْ) and it could mean overcoming, it could mean exalted, it could mean high,

511
00:38:56,810 --> 00:39:01,189
so all of the meanings are meanings, that were bad omen, to this Yahoodi(يهودي).

512
00:39:01,584 --> 00:39:03,874
فَمَا رَجَعَ حَتَّى فَتَحَ الله عَلَيْهْ

513
00:39:03,987 --> 00:39:07,888
By the time, he returned Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) has opened that fortress.

514
00:39:08,377 --> 00:39:10,589
As Rasool Allah ﷺ has promised.

515
00:39:11,405 --> 00:39:24,601
Some spotlights from the Battle of Khaybar(خيبر), examples of Sahabah رضي الله عنهم and other examples too.

516
00:39:25,374 --> 00:39:27,606
Examples of good and bad

517
00:39:28,459 --> 00:39:35,197
there was this man, who was doing a very good job in fighting, the enemies of Allah.

518
00:39:35,943 --> 00:39:40,410
Rasool Allah ﷺ pointed towards him and said, He is one of the people of hellfire.

519
00:39:41,179 --> 00:39:46,341
And this was kind of shocking, to the Sahabah(صحابه) because of the strength of this man,

520
00:39:46,381 --> 00:39:48,275
and the good work that he was doing.

521
00:39:48,484 --> 00:39:49,751
It say, in one narration;

522
00:39:49,775 --> 00:39:51,588
حَتَّى كَادَ بَعْضهُمْ اَنْ يَرْتَابْ

523
00:39:51,724 --> 00:39:53,674
Some of them were going to have doubts

524
00:39:54,162 --> 00:39:59,750
because on one hand, Rasool Allah ﷺ says that he is from the people of hellfire.

525
00:40:00,098 --> 00:40:04,385
And one hand they see a Mujahid(مجاهد) Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله) who is fighting.

526
00:40:04,955 --> 00:40:10,464
Atleast that's what, they see because, they don't know what's in the heart of this man.

527
00:40:10,882 --> 00:40:13,149
But they see that, he's very strong fighter,

528
00:40:13,551 --> 00:40:18,455
and these Sahabah(صحابه), they understood the Faza'el(فضائل), the virtues of fighting Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله)

529
00:40:18,532 --> 00:40:21,803
so they saw it, something very striking, and strange, ironic.

530
00:40:22,323 --> 00:40:25,581
So, one of them said: "I'm going to follow this man and see what happens."

531
00:40:25,605 --> 00:40:28,138
So, he speeds up, he would speed after him.

532
00:40:28,178 --> 00:40:30,284
If he slow down, he slow down after him.

533
00:40:30,401 --> 00:40:34,029
I mean, he's, he's trailing him, following him, wherever he goes.

534
00:40:34,494 --> 00:40:38,302
And then the man was injured, it was painful

535
00:40:38,532 --> 00:40:41,597
and the man did not have Sabr(صبر), did not have patience.

536
00:40:42,062 --> 00:40:46,518
So, he took an arrow from his quiver and he slit his throat.

537
00:40:47,046 --> 00:40:50,444
The Sahabah(صحابه), who saw that, went rushing to Rasool Allah ﷺ and said;

538
00:40:50,475 --> 00:40:53,367
O Rasool Ullah what you said, became true.

539
00:40:53,798 --> 00:40:54,911
Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

540
00:40:54,959 --> 00:41:03,118
قُمْ يَا فُلَانْ فَاَذَّنْ اَنَّه’ لَا يَدْخُلُ الْجَنَّةْ اِلَّا مُؤمِنْ وَاَنَّ اللهَ يُؤيدُ هَذَ الدِّيْنْ بِرَجُل فَاجِرْ

541
00:41:03,344 --> 00:41:10,052
Go and announce to everyone, that only a believer will enter into paradise.

542
00:41:10,181 --> 00:41:17,566
And that Allah could support this religion, through a corrupt person.

543
00:41:18,053 --> 00:41:24,207
This was a corrupt person who's deeds gave support to Islam because, he was a good fighter.

544
00:41:24,617 --> 00:41:32,397
So, definitely what he did, was supportive of Islam, even though he was a corrupt person.

545
00:41:32,675 --> 00:41:36,902
So, not everyone that is supporting the religion, is a believer,

546
00:41:37,172 --> 00:41:41,239
and then Rasool Allah ﷺ is saying announce to the people, and let them know

547
00:41:41,400 --> 00:41:44,076
that only the believer will enter into Jannah(جنة).

548
00:41:44,492 --> 00:41:52,338
So, not everybody whom you think, whom you see, as being good is a person that would go to Jannah(جنة).

549
00:41:52,656 --> 00:41:57,310
This doesn't mean that we should start doubting the intentions of people.

550
00:41:57,334 --> 00:41:59,084
No, that's not what is meant by this.

551
00:41:59,489 --> 00:42:06,400
But we cannot make a judgment for certain that such and, such person is in Jannah(جنة),

552
00:42:06,520 --> 00:42:08,760
 that's something that, we do not know.

553
00:42:09,541 --> 00:42:12,688
That is something that only Allahعَزّوجَلّ knows

554
00:42:13,160 --> 00:42:17,440
and we cannot judge and make a definite opinion

555
00:42:17,724 --> 00:42:20,384
that particular person is entering into Jannah(جنة)

556
00:42:20,409 --> 00:42:23,461
except if Rasool Allah ﷺ has given us that Shahadah(شهادة)

557
00:42:23,786 --> 00:42:26,201
such as the Shahadah(شهادة), he gave to the 10

558
00:42:26,627 --> 00:42:29,594
and the Shahadah(شهادة) that he gave to Bilal رضي الله عنه

559
00:42:29,729 --> 00:42:32,328
and the Shahadah(شهادة) that he gave to Abdullah Ibn Salam(عبدالله إبن سلام)

560
00:42:32,440 --> 00:42:36,837
and the Shahadah(شهادة) that he gave, some other Sahabah رضي الله عنهم.

561
00:42:38,099 --> 00:42:42,759
The next example there was a Bedouin, A'araabi(اعرابي) he became Muslim

562
00:42:43,068 --> 00:42:47,931
and then he went out with Rasool Allah ﷺ in the Battle of Khaybar(خيبر)

563
00:42:48,521 --> 00:42:51,656
the Muslims won in the Battle of Khaybar(خيبر) and it was a great booty.

564
00:42:51,965 --> 00:42:55,188
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ divided the booty among the Sahabah(صحابه)

565
00:42:55,450 --> 00:43:01,963
and after a long period of poverty now, they have something to live on.

566
00:43:02,116 --> 00:43:06,395
One of the best Ghanaem(غنائم) that, they ever had was the Ghaneemah(غنيمة) of Khaybar(خيبر).

567
00:43:06,806 --> 00:43:12,122
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ, told some Sahabah(صحابه) to take this and give it to the Bedouin.

568
00:43:12,400 --> 00:43:16,930
This is his share of the Ghaneemah(غنيمة), so his share was brought him.

569
00:43:17,567 --> 00:43:17,831
He said:

570
00:43:17,856 --> 00:43:18,384
 مَا هَذَا

571
00:43:18,423 --> 00:43:19,107
What is this?

572
00:43:19,529 --> 00:43:22,613
They said: This is your share of the booty.

573
00:43:22,939 --> 00:43:25,387
He went back to Rasool Allah ﷺ and said;

574
00:43:25,412 --> 00:43:25,936
 مَا هَذَا

575
00:43:25,975 --> 00:43:26,738
What is this?

576
00:43:26,762 --> 00:43:29,031
He was told, this was Ghaneemah(غنيمة) this is your share.

577
00:43:29,391 --> 00:43:29,701
He said;

578
00:43:29,741 --> 00:43:31,338
  مَا عَلَى هَذَا تَّبَعْتُكْ

579
00:43:31,669 --> 00:43:34,269
This is not why, I became Muslim and followed you.

580
00:43:34,562 --> 00:43:40,676
اِنَّمَا اتَّبَعْتُكَ عَلَى أن أرمى هَاهُنَا بِسَهْمٍ فَاَدْخُلُ الْجَنَّة، فَاُقْتَل فَاَدْخُلَ الْجَنَّة

581
00:43:40,723 --> 00:43:42,726
This is not why, I followed you.

582
00:43:43,330 --> 00:43:47,058
I followed you, so that I would be hit right here

583
00:43:47,246 --> 00:43:51,828
and he pointed to his neck with an arrow and then I would be killed

584
00:43:51,918 --> 00:43:53,915
and I would enter into paradise.

585
00:43:54,826 --> 00:43:55,774
Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله)

586
00:43:55,870 --> 00:43:59,663
look at the purity of his Fitrah(فطرة), Ghaneemah(غنيمة) is Halal(حلال) for him.

587
00:44:00,188 --> 00:44:03,262
I mean, it is in fact, the best of Rizq(رزق)

588
00:44:03,774 --> 00:44:08,470
because Allahعَزّوجَلّ has made Ghaneemah(غنيمة) the Rizq(رزق) of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

589
00:44:09,060 --> 00:44:12,112
Rasool Allah ﷺ was a shepherd before Prophet hood,

590
00:44:12,152 --> 00:44:14,601
and he was a businessman, before Prophet hood

591
00:44:14,626 --> 00:44:18,647
but after Nabuwwa(نبوة), his Rizq(رزق) came from the booties of war.

592
00:44:18,710 --> 00:44:25,721
He stopped working, he discontinued, his former professions and gave his time, full time,

593
00:44:26,194 --> 00:44:28,033
to spreading the Da'wah(دعوة) of Allah.

594
00:44:28,073 --> 00:44:29,453
 So, how did he survived.

595
00:44:29,628 --> 00:44:33,244
He survived through, his share of Al-Ghaneemah(ألغنيمه).

596
00:44:33,545 --> 00:44:35,462
Rasool Allah ﷺ says in the Hadith(حديث).

597
00:44:35,905 --> 00:44:41,253
بُعِثْتُ بِالسّيْفْ، بَيْنَ يَدَيِّ السَّاعَةْ، وَجُعِلَ رِزْقِي، تَحْتَ ظِلْ رُمْحِيْ

598
00:44:41,671 --> 00:44:44,593
I was sent with the sword, before the hour

599
00:44:44,775 --> 00:44:51,345
and my sustenance comes from under the shade, of my spear.

600
00:44:51,928 --> 00:44:55,857
So, if Allahعَزّوجَلّ has made it, the Rizq(رزق) of Rasool Ullah

601
00:44:55,897 --> 00:45:03,211
it is the best form, of sustenance according to the opinion of Ulema(علماء)

602
00:45:03,236 --> 00:45:06,444
such as Ibn Rajab Al-Hanbali(إبن رجب ألحنبلي), when he commented on this Hadith(حديث).

603
00:45:07,296 --> 00:45:11,032
So, it is the best form of Rizq(رزق) and this Bedouin said: I don't want it.

604
00:45:11,677 --> 00:45:17,038
Something that all of the Sahabah(صحابه) are accepting and he voluntarily said: I don't want this.

605
00:45:17,699 --> 00:45:20,503
So, this is a man, who's not looking for the bottom line

606
00:45:20,528 --> 00:45:24,219
this is a man whose heart has absorbed Islam

607
00:45:24,616 --> 00:45:30,345
 and he has reached to the level where he's only thinking about Jannah(جنة), he's only thinking about meeting Allah.

608
00:45:30,960 --> 00:45:34,723
and he is a Bedouin, simple man, who doesn't have a lot of knowledge

609
00:45:35,219 --> 00:45:39,334
but his Fitrah(فطرة) was clean he told Rasool Allah ﷺ.

610
00:45:39,358 --> 00:45:40,785
مَا عَلَى هَذَا اتَّبَعْتُكْ

611
00:45:40,810 --> 00:45:42,719
I did not followed you for this?

612
00:45:43,080 --> 00:45:47,094
I followed you, so said that, I would be struck with an arrow right here, and enter into Jannah(جنة)

613
00:45:48,297 --> 00:45:54,219
and then in another battle, Subhaan Allah(سبحان الله) well let's go back and see what Rasool Ullah said;

614
00:45:54,437 --> 00:45:57,120
When he made that statement, Rasool Allah ﷺ told him.

615
00:45:57,335 --> 00:45:59,331
اِنْ تَصدق الله يَصدق

616
00:45:59,546 --> 00:46:02,972
If you are true with Allah, Allah will fulfill what you want.

617
00:46:02,996 --> 00:46:04,064
Allah will be true with you.

618
00:46:04,104 --> 00:46:06,786
Meaning Allah will give you, what you desire?.

619
00:46:07,334 --> 00:46:11,176
And Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله), we find that all over in Qur'an and Hadith(حديث).

620
00:46:11,399 --> 00:46:13,220
وَالَّذِينَ اهْتَدَوْا زَادَهُمْ هُدًى

621
00:46:13,497 --> 00:46:15,972
The ones, who seek guidance, Allah will give it to them,

622
00:46:15,996 --> 00:46:18,599
وَالَّذِينَ جَاهَدُوا فِينَا لَنَهْدِيَنَّهُمْ سُبُلَنَا ۚ

623
00:46:18,758 --> 00:46:23,256
And the ones who struggle in Our path we will guide them to Our path.

624
00:46:23,392 --> 00:46:24,044
So,

625
00:46:24,124 --> 00:46:29,236
مَنْ تَقَرَّبَ إليَّ شِبْرًا تَقَرَّبْتُ إِلَيْهِ ذِرَاعًا، اِن مشيت إليَّ هَرْوَلَت إليَّك

626
00:46:29,261 --> 00:46:31,846
If you walk towards Allah, Allah will run towards you.

627
00:46:31,941 --> 00:46:33,316
So, it depends on your efforts.

628
00:46:33,522 --> 00:46:38,578
If you are truthful, with Allah, Rasool Allah ﷺ told him, Allah will be true with you.

629
00:46:39,424 --> 00:46:43,541
And this man you can see in his statement, truth.

630
00:46:44,428 --> 00:46:48,124
You can see honesty, you can see the willingness to sacrifice.

631
00:46:49,566 --> 00:46:57,055
In another battle he was hit with an arrow in the exact place, where he pointed his finger towards.

632
00:46:57,387 --> 00:47:00,215
So, he was brought to Rasool Allah ﷺ,

633
00:47:00,604 --> 00:47:03,177
and Rasool Allah ﷺ said: Is it him.?

634
00:47:03,503 --> 00:47:04,964
They said: Yes it is him.

635
00:47:05,804 --> 00:47:07,440
What did Rasool Allah ﷺ do?

636
00:47:07,851 --> 00:47:14,155
Rasool Allah ﷺ put his own garment over him, to be put with him in his grave.

637
00:47:14,441 --> 00:47:19,828
Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله) the garment, that has touched the skin of Rasool Allah ﷺ

638
00:47:20,058 --> 00:47:24,663
you know we talked about, the Sahabah(صحابه) would fight over the hair of Rasool Ullah

639
00:47:25,089 --> 00:47:30,213
and they would fight over, the droplets of Wadhoo(وضوء) that would fall from, his body

640
00:47:30,237 --> 00:47:32,590
so that they would rub it over their selves.

641
00:47:33,165 --> 00:47:36,409
They would fight, to get that blessing from Rasool Ullah,

642
00:47:36,675 --> 00:47:39,932
 and this Bedouin is getting it, without any effort.

643
00:47:40,262 --> 00:47:44,253
Rasool Allah ﷺ is wrapping him, in his own Garment.

644
00:47:44,335 --> 00:47:47,041
The garment that has touched, the skin of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

645
00:47:47,129 --> 00:47:52,514
And then Rasool Allah ﷺ put him in his grave and he made for him, a long Dua(دُعَا),

646
00:47:52,747 --> 00:47:56,325
the narrator of this Hadith(حديث), and this Hadith(حديث) is authentic, and it is in Al-Bayhaqi(البيهقي)

647
00:47:56,485 --> 00:47:58,408
The narrator of this, he said;

648
00:47:58,440 --> 00:48:03,486
The part that I remembered, or the part that I heard, from the Dua(دُعَا) of Rasool Allah ﷺ was;

649
00:48:03,643 --> 00:48:12,002
اَللَّهُمَّ هَذَا عَبْدُكَ خَرَجَ مُجَاهِدًا فِيْ سَبِيْلِكْ قُتِلَ شَهِيْدًا وَ اَنَا عَلَى ذَالِكَ شَهِيْدْ

650
00:48:12,809 --> 00:48:18,376
O Allah! This is Your servant, he came forth, Mujahid(مجاهد),

651
00:48:18,591 --> 00:48:26,303
struggling, in Your path, and he was killed as a Shaheed(شهيد) and I am a witness of that,

652
00:48:26,724 --> 00:48:28,355
Allah-Ho-Akbar(الله اكبر), Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله),

653
00:48:28,506 --> 00:48:33,882
Rasool Allah ﷺ is saying I'm a witness that, this man is Mujahid(مجاهد) and he is a Shaheed(شهيد).

654
00:48:34,130 --> 00:48:37,807
What a better witness, what a great badge of honor,

655
00:48:38,209 --> 00:48:41,951
that was given to this simple Bedouin, with little knowledge

656
00:48:41,975 --> 00:48:46,706
but because of his Sidq(صدق), because of his truth, he was rewarded this great reward.

657
00:48:48,083 --> 00:48:53,111
The next example Abu'l Yussr(أبولْيُسْر), a companion of Rasool Allah ﷺ, he said;

658
00:48:53,135 --> 00:48:55,389
اِنِّيْ لَمع رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم بِخَيْبَرْ

659
00:48:55,413 --> 00:49:00,136
I was with Rasool Allah ﷺ in Khaybar(خيبر), one day.

660
00:49:00,539 --> 00:49:03,681
اِذْ اَقْبَلَتْ غَنَمْ لِرَجُلِ مِنْ اليَهُوْدْ تُرِيْدُ حصنَهُمْ

661
00:49:03,990 --> 00:49:09,521
When we saw sheep belonging to one of the Yahood(يهود)

662
00:49:09,994 --> 00:49:13,566
and the sheep were entering into their fortress.

663
00:49:13,883 --> 00:49:16,319
And we were besieging that fortress.

664
00:49:17,128 --> 00:49:22,117
So Rasool Allah ﷺ saw this sheep and the Muslims apparently were hungry.

665
00:49:22,464 --> 00:49:23,910
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

666
00:49:23,934 --> 00:49:27,288
مَنْ الرَجُلْ يُطْعِمُنَا مِنْ هَذِهِ الْغَنَمْ

667
00:49:27,808 --> 00:49:34,632
Who will feed us from these sheep, Abu'l Yussr(أبولْيُسْر) said: Me, O Messenger of Allah!

668
00:49:34,656 --> 00:49:36,662
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: then go ahead.

669
00:49:36,995 --> 00:49:39,634
قَاَلَ فَخَرَجْتُ اَشْتَدْ مِثْلَ الظَلِيْمْ

670
00:49:39,658 --> 00:49:42,470
I set out running like an ostrich.

671
00:49:43,092 --> 00:49:47,517
Now, Al-Zaleem(ألظليم) is the name that, the Arabs give to the male ostrich.

672
00:49:47,879 --> 00:49:51,077
The ostrich used to live in the Arabian Peninsula.

673
00:49:51,185 --> 00:49:57,792
It was indigenous to the Arabian peninsula but now it became extinct Allah-Ho-Alam(الله اعلم), when

674
00:49:57,832 --> 00:50:03,950
 but we don't hear from any of our forefathers that they have seen any ostriches.

675
00:50:03,974 --> 00:50:07,793
So, my it must have been a while, since they ran extinct.

676
00:50:08,094 --> 00:50:15,211
But there's a lot of poetry and stories from old Arabia that talk about the ostrich.

677
00:50:15,616 --> 00:50:17,581
They used to eat, the eggs of the ostrich

678
00:50:17,605 --> 00:50:20,370
and also, they used to feed on, its flesh and it's Halal(حلال)

679
00:50:20,869 --> 00:50:26,388
and they also used the feathers of ostrich were very expensive and

680
00:50:27,110 --> 00:50:32,312
fighters, the knights used to decorate their armor with feathers of the ostrich

681
00:50:32,694 --> 00:50:38,900
and you might have heard that Hamza Bin Abdul Muttalib رضي الله عنه in the battle of Uhud(أحَد) had an ostrich feather,

682
00:50:39,202 --> 00:50:44,448
also in Badr(بدر) he had an ostrich feather on his chest, decorating his chest.

683
00:50:44,878 --> 00:50:46,760
And the ostrich is very fast.

684
00:50:47,410 --> 00:50:56,221
They say that the speed of an ostrich could reach to between 65 kilometers per hour to eighty kilometers per hour, it's pretty fast.

685
00:50:56,565 --> 00:51:02,342
So, this Sahabi(صحابي), he said: I set out running like an ostrich, meaning that he was very fast.

686
00:51:03,184 --> 00:51:09,681
فَلَمَّا نَظَرَ اِلَيَّ رَسُوْل الله صلى الله عليه وسلم موَلِّيَّا، قَالَ اَللَّهُمَّ اَمْتِعْنَا بِهْ

687
00:51:10,074 --> 00:51:17,229
And when Rasool Allah ﷺ saw me running, he said: O Allah! Let us enjoy his company.

688
00:51:17,710 --> 00:51:19,333
قَالَ فَاَدركْتُ الْغَنَمْ

689
00:51:19,358 --> 00:51:25,860
So, I reached to the sheep, when the first of them have already entered the fortress.

690
00:51:25,884 --> 00:51:30,203
So he, only was able to catch the last of them.

691
00:51:30,228 --> 00:51:31,996
فَاَخَذْتُ شَائتَيْـنْ مِنْ اُخْرَهَاَ

692
00:51:32,020 --> 00:51:33,356
So, he took two of them,

693
00:51:33,381 --> 00:51:34,867
فَاخْتَزَمْتُهَا تَحْتَ يَدَيْ

694
00:51:34,891 --> 00:51:37,418
So, I hug them, under my arms,

695
00:51:37,596 --> 00:51:41,118
ثُمَّ جِئْتْ بِهِمَا اَشْتَدْ كَاَنَّ هُوْلَيْسَ مَعِيْ شَيْء

696
00:51:41,295 --> 00:51:44,675
And I came back running, as if I was carrying nothing with me.

697
00:51:44,824 --> 00:51:49,397
Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله) running, while he's holding two of these sheep, he said;

698
00:51:49,421 --> 00:51:52,618
I was so light in my running as if, I had nothing with me.

699
00:51:53,196 --> 00:51:56,688
حَتَّى اَلْقَيْتُهُمَاَ  عِنْدَ رَسُوْل الله صلى الله عليه وسلم

700
00:51:56,767 --> 00:51:59,537
Until I dropped them, under the feet of Rasool Ullah.

701
00:51:59,864 --> 00:52:01,650
فَذَبَحوْهُمَا فَاَكَلُوْهُمَا

702
00:52:01,675 --> 00:52:04,039
They slaughtered them and they had a feast.

703
00:52:04,488 --> 00:52:09,492
فَكَانَ اَبُو الْيُسْرْ مَنْ آخِرِ اَصَحَابِ رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم مَوْتَا

704
00:52:09,516 --> 00:52:13,538
Abu'l Yussr(أبولْيُسْر) was one of the last of the Sahabah(صحابه) to die. Why?

705
00:52:14,028 --> 00:52:16,082
because of the Dua(دُعَا) of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

706
00:52:16,446 --> 00:52:19,018
Rasool Allah said: O Allah, let us enjoy his company.

707
00:52:19,529 --> 00:52:25,386
Abu'l Yussr(أبو الْيُسْر) when he would mentioned this Hadith(حديث), he would cry, he would say;

708
00:52:25,411 --> 00:52:29,184
أمتعوا بي لعمري حتى كنت آخرهم موتا

709
00:52:29,567 --> 00:52:35,896
They enjoyed my company until, I became the last of them, one of the last of them to die.

710
00:52:36,197 --> 00:52:40,213
He was kind of sad that he was, the one left behind

711
00:52:40,499 --> 00:52:45,361
while all of his friends and Rasool Allah ﷺ have passed away before him.

712
00:52:46,291 --> 00:52:52,341
Then we have the incident that occurred with Abdullah Bin Mughaffal رضي الله عنه, one of the companions.

713
00:52:52,844 --> 00:52:58,249
When they opened one of the fortresses in Khyber(خيبر), they found dried fat.

714
00:52:58,895 --> 00:53:05,506
Fat of animals, they would cut it into pieces, and they would dry it in the sun, for future use.

715
00:53:05,870 --> 00:53:09,974
So, there was a sack filled with this dried fat

716
00:53:10,475 --> 00:53:14,849
and Abdullah Bin Mughaffal(عبدالله بن مُغَفَّل) grabbed it and he put it on his shoulder.

717
00:53:15,086 --> 00:53:19,312
He started walking with it towards his company to feed on it.

718
00:53:19,529 --> 00:53:25,318
So, they must have been quite hungry and without sufficient food.

719
00:53:25,574 --> 00:53:31,658
Now, the man responsible for dividing the booty

720
00:53:31,844 --> 00:53:34,894
he saw Abdullah Bin Mughaffal(عبدالله بن مُغَفَّل) walking away with this sack

721
00:53:35,284 --> 00:53:38,585
he walked up to him, and he held the sack from one end.

722
00:53:38,658 --> 00:53:44,460
And he tried to pull it away and saying give it to me, so that it be split among the Muslims.

723
00:53:44,533 --> 00:53:49,595
I mean, according to the laws of, the laws and regulations of dividing, the booty.

724
00:53:50,114 --> 00:53:51,928
Abdullah Bin Mughaffal(عبدالله بن مُغَفَّل), refused.

725
00:53:51,952 --> 00:53:56,739
So, they were pulling Abdullah Bin Mughaffal(عبدالله بن مُغَفَّل) is pulling from one end

726
00:53:56,764 --> 00:54:00,766
and this other companion is pulling from the other end, it's tugging between them

727
00:54:00,900 --> 00:54:03,439
and Rasool Allah ﷺ saw this and smiled

728
00:54:04,008 --> 00:54:07,218
and then Rasool Allah ﷺ, told the man responsible for the Ghaneemah(غنيمة)

729
00:54:07,260 --> 00:54:10,226
just let him go, Leave, Leave it, let him take it.

730
00:54:10,260 --> 00:54:10,972
لَا اَذَالَكْ

731
00:54:10,996 --> 00:54:12,717
Just let him, have it.

732
00:54:13,138 --> 00:54:15,637
And Rasool Allah ﷺ was laughing at Abdullah Bin Mughaffal(عبدالله بن مُغَفَّل).

733
00:54:15,662 --> 00:54:18,601
Abdullah Bin Mughaffal(عبدالله بن مُغَفَّل) said: I was quite embarrassed by that

734
00:54:18,705 --> 00:54:23,084
 and having this incident happened in front of Rasool Allah ﷺ it's quite embarrassing

735
00:54:23,438 --> 00:54:27,171
but he said I took it away, and I went to my companions and we ate it all.

736
00:54:27,809 --> 00:54:30,940
The scholars derived from this, a Hukum(حكم) that

737
00:54:30,964 --> 00:54:35,193
you're allowed to eat from Ghaneemah(غنيمة) food on the spot

738
00:54:35,669 --> 00:54:37,820
 but not take anything with you back,

739
00:54:38,590 --> 00:54:48,788
 gold, silver, weapons all that other valuables need to be put with Al-Ghaneemah(الغنيمة) clothes and they need to be split

740
00:54:49,148 --> 00:54:53,698
and the punishment for taking from Al-Ghaneemah(الغنيمة) is very severe.

741
00:54:54,071 --> 00:54:57,744
however Rasool Allah ﷺ allowed Abdullah Bin Mughaffal(عبدالله بن مُغَفَّل) to have this

742
00:54:57,970 --> 00:55:01,748
because as the scholars have derive the Hukum(حكم) that food is exception.

743
00:55:01,781 --> 00:55:07,059
You were allowed to eat, but not take anything with you, all you can eat just like a buffet

744
00:55:07,334 --> 00:55:10,015
all you can eat but you're not allowed to take anything out of the restaurant.

745
00:55:11,004 --> 00:55:14,127
And then we have the Al-Mar'a Al-Ghafariyyah(ألمَرْأةِ الْغَفاريه).

746
00:55:14,486 --> 00:55:19,824
And this story is mentioned Ibn Is'haqq(اِبْنِ اِسْحَاقْ), she's mentioning her story.

747
00:55:20,008 --> 00:55:25,062
She said: I came to Rasool Allah ﷺ along with some women from Ghaffar(غفار).

748
00:55:25,184 --> 00:55:28,623
Ghaffar(غفار) were Bedouins, who were close to Madina

749
00:55:29,149 --> 00:55:36,447
and they were famous for stealing pilgrims, that was their reputation in Arabia before Islam.

750
00:55:37,048 --> 00:55:39,778
They would attack the pilgrims and rob them.

751
00:55:40,562 --> 00:55:43,396
Many of them became Muslim and eventually all of them became Muslim

752
00:55:43,436 --> 00:55:48,806
because of the Barakah(بركة) of the Da'wah(دعوة) of Abu Dhar Al-Ghaffari رضي الله عنه.

753
00:55:48,831 --> 00:55:54,347
So a tribe was such a bad reputation, nevertheless, Allahعَزّوجَلّ guided them. So,

754
00:55:54,371 --> 00:55:55,468
الله يَهْدِيْ مَنْ يَشَآء

755
00:55:55,492 --> 00:55:57,053
Allah guides whomever, He wills.

756
00:55:58,929 --> 00:56:05,572
This woman came to Rasool Allah ﷺ and she came with some other women from Ghaffar(غفار)

757
00:56:05,596 --> 00:56:09,357
and she told Rasool Allah ﷺ, we want to go forth with you

758
00:56:09,923 --> 00:56:16,864
in order that we can take care of the wounded and attend to the other needs of the Muslims.

759
00:56:17,585 --> 00:56:18,986
Rasool Allah ﷺ told her;

760
00:56:19,010 --> 00:56:20,104
عَلَى بَرَكَة االله

761
00:56:20,508 --> 00:56:22,119
Go with the blessing of Allah.

762
00:56:22,350 --> 00:56:25,581
He allowed her to, accompany him

763
00:56:26,074 --> 00:56:30,294
and Rasool Allah ﷺ not only allowed them to accompany the army

764
00:56:30,384 --> 00:56:35,341
but Rasool Allah ﷺ had this young girl, ride on the same camel with him.

765
00:56:35,447 --> 00:56:37,969
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ was sitting on Rahal(رحل), the seat

766
00:56:38,223 --> 00:56:44,141
and then behind him, was the luggage and he had her sit on top of the luggage

767
00:56:44,302 --> 00:56:49,856
She was a young girl then, now they arrived, their destination and the camel sat down

768
00:56:50,266 --> 00:56:58,904
and this girl came down from the camel, to see that on the luggage was some blood of hers.

769
00:56:59,947 --> 00:57:07,206
So, she sat curled, she curled herself next to the camel and she was, so embarrassed.

770
00:57:07,585 --> 00:57:13,518
This was her first period, she was quite embarrassed by what happened

771
00:57:14,034 --> 00:57:16,707
because of the blood on the luggage of Rasool Allah ﷺ

772
00:57:16,740 --> 00:57:19,179
and she just sat there next to the camel doing nothing.

773
00:57:19,647 --> 00:57:24,974
When Rasool Allah ﷺ saw that she was upset and then he also saw the blood on the luggage.

774
00:57:24,999 --> 00:57:25,517
So he said;

775
00:57:25,557 --> 00:57:27,267
 مَا لَكِ لَعَلَّكِ نَفِسْت

776
00:57:27,639 --> 00:57:31,624
What's wrong with you, have you had, your period?

777
00:57:31,800 --> 00:57:32,836
She said: Yes,

778
00:57:33,312 --> 00:57:36,669
Rasool Allah ﷺ told her: Clean yourself

779
00:57:37,005 --> 00:57:40,166
and take a vessel of water and put some salt in it.

780
00:57:40,561 --> 00:57:46,003
And then wipe out the blood from the baggage

781
00:57:46,063 --> 00:57:51,592
so use water with salt, clean the blood from the luggage.

782
00:57:51,835 --> 00:57:53,330
So, she said: She did that.

783
00:57:53,838 --> 00:57:57,614
And then we participated with Rasool Allah ﷺ in the battle.

784
00:57:57,876 --> 00:58:00,375
And when the booty was divided.

785
00:58:00,935 --> 00:58:08,768
Now, the Ulema(علماء) say that women and children are not given a share of the booty

786
00:58:09,237 --> 00:58:11,179
even if they join in fighting.

787
00:58:11,589 --> 00:58:14,815
But the Ameer(أمير) of the army can give them, what's called Radha(رضى)

788
00:58:15,101 --> 00:58:17,777
he can give them something but it's not equal to the share.

789
00:58:17,802 --> 00:58:23,420
He can give them what he sees appropriate but there are not counted as exact shares.

790
00:58:23,839 --> 00:58:28,287
So, she said Rasool Allah ﷺ called me and he had the necklace with him.

791
00:58:28,901 --> 00:58:32,445
And he gave me the necklace and said: This is yours.

792
00:58:32,746 --> 00:58:37,786
And she said: He with his own hands, put it around my neck.

793
00:58:38,270 --> 00:58:43,162
Now, after that, she said: Whenever I would have menstrual period

794
00:58:43,805 --> 00:58:47,305
I would always wash myself with water and salt.

795
00:58:48,122 --> 00:58:55,189
And in fact, in her will she asked that she should be washed with water and salt.

796
00:58:55,685 --> 00:59:01,278
And she said: In the name of Allah, In the name of Allah,

797
00:59:01,728 --> 00:59:09,220
I will never apart with this necklace that was put around my neck by the own hands of Rasool Allah ﷺ

798
00:59:09,601 --> 00:59:13,541
and when she died, the necklace was left on her neck.

799
00:59:14,955 --> 00:59:20,493
I'm going to leave this story as it is without tampering with it, with my own comments.

800
00:59:20,934 --> 00:59:24,624
I think it's beautiful enough to leave as it is

801
00:59:25,021 --> 00:59:36,647
 for you to drive the amazing examples of companionship and love that the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم had for Rasool Allah ﷺ

802
00:59:37,001 --> 00:59:42,849
and I means Rasool Allah ﷺ did not tell her to permanently use salt for cleansing,

803
00:59:43,118 --> 00:59:48,148
she did that out of love of Rasool Allah ﷺ, she did that to remember Rasool Allah ﷺ.

804
00:59:48,582 --> 00:59:52,760
Rasool Ullah did not tell her to wash herself when she dies with water and salt

805
00:59:53,112 --> 00:59:57,663
but she did that because of the memories of Rasool Allah ﷺ that she had

806
00:59:57,972 --> 01:00:03,923
and the whole story of Rasool Allah ﷺ calling her and allowing her to ride with him on a same mount,

807
01:00:04,043 --> 01:00:12,183
she was a young girl and the fact that she offered her help and she's at that young age and she's a Bedouin woman

808
01:00:12,505 --> 01:00:16,687
the love that they had for Islam, the love that they had for Rasool Allah ﷺ

809
01:00:17,121 --> 01:00:20,071
the willingness to sacrifice, the willingness to help.

810
01:00:20,309 --> 01:00:24,580
Where are these meanings now, we have lost a lot of these meanings

811
01:00:24,928 --> 01:00:30,076
and, the embarrassment that she had when she would have her first period

812
01:00:30,291 --> 01:00:36,123
because she messed up with the luggage of Rasool Allah ﷺ, so she was so ashamed of that

813
01:00:36,666 --> 01:00:41,003
and the kindness of Rasool Allah ﷺ and the instructions that he gave her

814
01:00:41,367 --> 01:00:45,562
and then the fact that Rasool Allah ﷺ would call her, after that and remember her

815
01:00:45,895 --> 01:00:50,883
and she is just a member of this large army following Rasool Allah ﷺ.

816
01:00:51,206 --> 01:00:53,844
He calls this girl by name

817
01:00:54,353 --> 01:00:58,433
and he has a necklace and he puts it around her neck with his own hands

818
01:00:59,081 --> 01:01:02,762
the gratitude that Rasool Allah ﷺ had for his companions

819
01:01:03,102 --> 01:01:05,173
and the love and attention that he gave them

820
01:01:06,052 --> 01:01:09,324
all of these are wonderful and amazing examples.

821
01:01:09,349 --> 01:01:14,557
I think there's a lot to learn from the story if we would contemplate and think about it

822
01:01:14,582 --> 01:01:17,498
and that's how we should deal with the Seerah(سيرة) of Rasool Allah ﷺ,

823
01:01:17,522 --> 01:01:20,258
we should not just listen to the stories to entertain ourselves

824
01:01:20,282 --> 01:01:21,752
we should learn the lessons from them.

825
01:01:22,869 --> 01:01:26,753
Then we have the story of the two Jewish women.

826
01:01:27,250 --> 01:01:29,844
The first is the Zainab Bint Al-Haris(زينب بنت حارث)

827
01:01:30,439 --> 01:01:34,265
this woman belongs to the nobility of Al-Yahood(أليهود)

828
01:01:34,644 --> 01:01:38,949
after the Battle of Khaybar(خيبر) and the defeat Al-Yahood(أليهود)

829
01:01:39,390 --> 01:01:42,612
she held an invitation Waleema(وليمه).

830
01:01:43,014 --> 01:01:48,724
She hosted Rasool Allah ﷺ and some of the Sahabah(صحابه) and she roasted for them a sheep

831
01:01:49,438 --> 01:01:55,452
and, she filled it, with poison and she asked about the particular parts

832
01:01:55,785 --> 01:02:02,042
that Rasool Allah ﷺ loves and she added, the poison in those pieces

833
01:02:02,866 --> 01:02:04,837
Rasool Allah ﷺ accepted the Da'wah(دعوة),

834
01:02:04,861 --> 01:02:07,584
he accepted the invitation and he came with the Sahabah(صحابه)

835
01:02:08,313 --> 01:02:12,020
and she offered them, their meal and they started eating.

836
01:02:12,805 --> 01:02:18,731
Bishr Bin Al-Bara'a(بشر بن البراء), he was the first to swallow a bite from this meat.

837
01:02:19,087 --> 01:02:24,356
Rasool Allah ﷺ had the meat in his mouth but he's didn't swallow it yet.

838
01:02:24,829 --> 01:02:30,722
And then Rasool Allah ﷺ dropped it and he said: This bone is telling me that it's poisoned

839
01:02:31,687 --> 01:02:36,245
and then he called the woman and asked her and he said;

840
01:02:36,285 --> 01:02:39,085
Did you poison this for me? She said: Yes.

841
01:02:39,148 --> 01:02:40,456
He said: Why did he do so?

842
01:02:40,858 --> 01:02:46,337
She said: If you're a king then you would be killed and we would be at rest

843
01:02:46,935 --> 01:02:49,876
because we have ridden ourselves from you

844
01:02:50,606 --> 01:02:55,537
but if you were a Prophets Allah will tell you and you would know about it

845
01:02:56,252 --> 01:02:57,655
and then Rasool Allah ﷺ told her;

846
01:02:57,679 --> 01:02:59,670
مَا كَانَ الله لِيسلطك عَلَيْهْ

847
01:02:59,948 --> 01:03:05,689
Allah سبحانه وتعالى would not give you the ability to overcome me, or to kill me

848
01:03:06,240 --> 01:03:09,201
and Rasool Allah ﷺ forgave her.

849
01:03:09,225 --> 01:03:11,914
The Sahabah(صحابه) said: Should we kill her, he said: No, leave her.

850
01:03:11,939 --> 01:03:17,272
But then Bishr Bin Al-Bara'a(بشر بن البراء) died because of the mouthful what he had

851
01:03:17,312 --> 01:03:19,174
 so, it shows you that this was powerful poison.

852
01:03:19,969 --> 01:03:25,000
So in some narrations it says that Rasool Allah ﷺ ordered that she be executed.

853
01:03:25,911 --> 01:03:28,671
Rasool Allah ﷺ survived for three years after that

854
01:03:29,698 --> 01:03:33,133
and in his final days, when he was suffering from fever

855
01:03:33,927 --> 01:03:37,641
and this Hadith(حديث) is in Bukhari(بخاريْ). Ayesha رضي الله عنها said;

856
01:03:37,672 --> 01:03:41,747
كَانَ النَّبِيُّ صلى الله عليه وسلم يَقُوْلُ فِيْ مَرْضِهِ الَّذِيْ مَاتَ فِيْهِ

857
01:03:41,923 --> 01:03:47,385
يا عائشه: مَا اَزال اَجد اَلَمَ الطَّعَامِ الَّذِي اَكَلتُ بِخَيْبَر

858
01:03:47,506 --> 01:03:51,902
فهذا أوان وجدت انقطاع أبهرى من ذلك السم

859
01:03:52,832 --> 01:03:55,906
Ayesha رضي الله عنها said: Rasool Allah ﷺ would say;

860
01:03:56,003 --> 01:04:00,783
In his final days in the disease that he died because of.

861
01:04:00,983 --> 01:04:05,671
O Ayesha(عائشه), I still find the taste of the food that I ate in khaybar(خيبر).

862
01:04:06,128 --> 01:04:11,234
This is the time when my Ab'hur(أبحر) would be cut, because of that poison.

863
01:04:11,543 --> 01:04:19,263
Abhurr(أبحر) is an artery, I think it's called in English aorta, believe it's spelled A O R T A

864
01:04:19,696 --> 01:04:25,269
and Rasool Allah ﷺ said: This is the time I feel that my Ab'hur(أبحر) will be cut

865
01:04:25,414 --> 01:04:27,992
because of the poison I had in khaybar(خيبر).

866
01:04:28,332 --> 01:04:29,523
Ibn Hishaam(إبن هشام) says;

867
01:04:29,909 --> 01:04:36,610
فَاِنْ كَانَ الْمُسْلِمُوْنَ لَيَرَوْنْ اَنَّ رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم مَاتَ شَهِيْدًا، مَعَ مَا اَكْرَمَه اللهُ مِنَّ النَّبُوَّة

868
01:04:36,787 --> 01:04:41,827
The Muslims see that Rasool Allah ﷺ died as a Shaheed(شهيد) in addition to being a Prophet,

869
01:04:41,932 --> 01:04:48,959
so Allah combined for Rasool Allah ﷺ the status of Prophet hood and the status of Shahadah(شهادة), martyrdom.

870
01:04:49,327 --> 01:04:53,558
Now some might see, this as contradicting, the fact that Allah promised Rasool Allah ﷺ

871
01:04:53,597 --> 01:04:55,129
وَاللَّهُ يَعْصِمُكَ مِنَ النَّاسِ ۗ

872
01:04:55,153 --> 01:04:56,928
Allah will protect you from people,

873
01:04:57,033 --> 01:04:58,138
so some scholars said:

874
01:04:58,397 --> 01:05:01,847
That the Allah did promise Rasool Allah ﷺ that He will protect them from Fitnah(فِتْنَه)

875
01:05:02,232 --> 01:05:04,407
He will protect him from defeat

876
01:05:04,833 --> 01:05:11,774
and He will protect him from being killed before, he fulfills his mission.

877
01:05:11,950 --> 01:05:16,195
And when Ayah(آية) was revealed that Allah has completed your religion for you,

878
01:05:16,219 --> 01:05:20,673
now it was time for Rasool Allah ﷺ, to leave this Duniyah(دُنِيَّا) and meet his Lord.

879
01:05:20,934 --> 01:05:27,281
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ died because of this poison, even though it was three years later,

880
01:05:27,306 --> 01:05:30,622
because as Rasool Allah ﷺ said that

881
01:05:30,741 --> 01:05:38,161
he told the woman that you would not have the ability to overpower me, being the Messenger of Allah,

882
01:05:38,861 --> 01:05:44,176
but the pain and the effect of the poison came three years later

883
01:05:44,274 --> 01:05:48,472
when it was already the appointed time for Rasool Allah ﷺ to pass away.

884
01:05:48,843 --> 01:05:52,854
This is the opinion of some of the Ulema'a(علماء) based on the authentic Ahadith(احاديث),

885
01:05:53,108 --> 01:05:56,276
one of them which I just narrated it, to you from Al-Bukhari(ألبخاري).

886
01:05:57,123 --> 01:05:59,571
The next woman is Safiyyah(صفيه)

887
01:05:59,786 --> 01:06:03,988
and In Sha' Allah(اِنْ شَاءالله) we'll leave that to our next session Be-iznillah(بإذن الله).

888
01:06:04,421 --> 01:06:08,871
صَلَّى الله عَلى سَيَّدِنَا محمد وَعَلى اَلِهِ وَ صَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ تَسْلِيْمًا كَثِيْرًا

